PathwayData.put("data/reading_writing/units/L03U6.json",{"strand":"reading_writing","level":3,"cefr":"A2a","unit":6,"theme":"Earth and Sky","essential_question":"What can we see in the sky, and why does it change?","schema_version":"1.0","core_words":["moon","stars","planet","Earth","orbit","day","night","shadow","crescent","space","rocket","astronaut","spin","light"],"recycled_words":["sun","night","day","stars","because","but","both","fact","opinion","for example","glossary","month","crescent"],"rubrics":[{"id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","title":"Analytic writing rubric","traits":[{"name":"Ideas","name_ar":"الأفكار","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear, interesting and fully developed with strong details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة وممتعة ومدعومة بتفاصيل قوية."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"My ideas are clear and have enough details.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري واضحة ومعها تفاصيل كافية."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"My main idea is there but needs more details.","descriptor_ar":"فكرتي الرئيسية موجودة لكنها تحتاج إلى تفاصيل أكثر."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"My ideas are unclear or very few.","descriptor_ar":"أفكاري غير واضحة أو قليلة جدًا."}]},{"name":"Organization","name_ar":"التنظيم","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Clear beginning, middle and end; ideas flow with linking words.","descriptor_ar":"بداية ووسط ونهاية واضحة، والأفكار مترابطة بكلمات الربط."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Clear order with some linking words.","descriptor_ar":"ترتيب واضح مع بعض كلمات الربط."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Some order, but parts are mixed up.","descriptor_ar":"يوجد بعض الترتيب لكن بعض الأجزاء غير مرتبة."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Ideas are not in order.","descriptor_ar":"الأفكار غير مرتبة."}]},{"name":"Vocabulary","name_ar":"المفردات","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"I use exact, varied words, including new unit words, correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات دقيقة ومتنوعة، منها كلمات الوحدة الجديدة، بشكل صحيح."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"I use some new words correctly.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم بعض الكلمات الجديدة بشكل صحيح."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"I use simple words; some are repeated or wrong.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات بسيطة، وبعضها مكرر أو غير صحيح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"I use very few words; the meaning is hard to understand.","descriptor_ar":"أستخدم كلمات قليلة جدًا ويصعب فهم المعنى."}]},{"name":"Sentence fluency","name_ar":"سلاسة الجمل","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"My sentences are complete, varied in length and easy to read aloud.","descriptor_ar":"جملي كاملة ومتنوعة الطول وسهلة القراءة بصوت عالٍ."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"Most sentences are complete, with some variety.","descriptor_ar":"معظم جملي كاملة مع بعض التنويع."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Many sentences are short or start the same way.","descriptor_ar":"كثير من جملي قصيرة أو تبدأ بالطريقة نفسها."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Sentences are incomplete or run together.","descriptor_ar":"جملي ناقصة أو متداخلة."}]},{"name":"Conventions","name_ar":"قواعد الكتابة","bands":[{"score":4,"descriptor":"Capitals, punctuation, spelling and grammar are almost always correct.","descriptor_ar":"الحروف الكبيرة وعلامات الترقيم والإملاء والقواعد صحيحة دائمًا تقريبًا."},{"score":3,"descriptor":"A few mistakes that do not affect meaning.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء قليلة لا تؤثر في المعنى."},{"score":2,"descriptor":"Several mistakes; the meaning is sometimes unclear.","descriptor_ar":"عدة أخطاء، والمعنى أحيانًا غير واضح."},{"score":1,"descriptor":"Many mistakes make it hard to read.","descriptor_ar":"أخطاء كثيرة تجعل القراءة صعبة."}]}]}],"lessons":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS1","title":"Word Power: Earth and Sky","lesson_type":"vocabulary","objectives":["read, say and use 14 words about Earth and space and 3 Tier 2 words (observe, contrast, phase)","use a glossary to find the meaning of bold science words","explain day and night and the Moon's shape using science words"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة ونطق واستخدام 14 كلمة عن الأرض والفضاء و3 كلمات أكاديمية (observe, contrast, phase).","استخدام المسرد لإيجاد معاني الكلمات العلمية الغامقة.","شرح الليل والنهار وشكل القمر بكلمات علمية."],"success_criteria":["I can read and use the space words in sentences.","I can find a word in a glossary using ABC order.","I can explain what spin and orbit mean."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع قراءة كلمات الفضاء واستخدامها في جمل.","أستطيع إيجاد كلمة في المسرد باستخدام الترتيب الأبجدي.","أستطيع شرح معنى spin وorbit."],"map_area":"Vocabulary: Acquisition and Use","vocabulary":[{"word":"moon","pos":"noun","ipa":"/mun/","definition":"the round object that goes around the Earth and shines at night","arabic":"القمر","example":"The moon is bright tonight.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"stars","pos":"noun","ipa":"/stɑrz/","definition":"huge balls of burning gas that look like small lights in the night sky","arabic":"النجوم","example":"We saw many stars in the desert.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"planet","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈplænɪt/","definition":"a very large round object that moves around the Sun","arabic":"كوكب","example":"Earth is a planet.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"Earth","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɝθ/","definition":"the planet we live on","arabic":"الأرض (الكوكب)","example":"Earth has land and oceans.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"orbit","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/ˈɔrbɪt/","definition":"to travel around another object in space; the path it takes","arabic":"يدور حول / مدار","example":"The Moon orbits the Earth.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"day","pos":"noun","ipa":"/deɪ/","definition":"the time when it is light; also a full 24 hours","arabic":"النهار / اليوم","example":"It is day when our side of Earth faces the Sun.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"night","pos":"noun","ipa":"/naɪt/","definition":"the time when it is dark","arabic":"الليل","example":"It is night when our side of Earth faces away from the Sun.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V07","tier":"core"},{"word":"shadow","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃædoʊ/","definition":"a dark shape made when something blocks light","arabic":"ظل","example":"My shadow is long in the evening.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V08","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V08","tier":"core"},{"word":"crescent","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkrɛsənt/","definition":"the thin, curved shape of the new moon","arabic":"هلال","example":"We saw the crescent moon at the start of Ramadan.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V09","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V09","tier":"core"},{"word":"space","pos":"noun","ipa":"/speɪs/","definition":"the area outside Earth where the planets and stars are","arabic":"الفضاء","example":"Astronauts travel to space.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V10","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V10","tier":"core"},{"word":"rocket","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɑkɪt/","definition":"a vehicle that flies into space","arabic":"صاروخ","example":"The rocket roared into the sky.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V11","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V11","tier":"core"},{"word":"astronaut","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈæstrənɔt/","definition":"a person who travels into space","arabic":"رائد فضاء","example":"The astronaut floated in the space station.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V12","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V12","tier":"core"},{"word":"spin","pos":"verb","ipa":"/spɪn/","definition":"to turn around and around very fast","arabic":"يدور حول نفسه","example":"The Earth spins once every day.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V13","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V13","tier":"core"},{"word":"light","pos":"noun","ipa":"/laɪt/","definition":"what makes it possible to see; it comes from the Sun or a lamp","arabic":"ضوء","example":"The Moon reflects the Sun's light.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V14","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V14","tier":"core"},{"word":"observe","pos":"verb","ipa":"/əbˈzɝv/","definition":"to watch carefully to learn something","arabic":"يرصد / يلاحظ","example":"Observe the Moon every night for a week.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V15","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V15","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"contrast","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/kənˈtræst/","definition":"to show how things are different; a difference","arabic":"يقارن بالتباين / تباين","example":"Contrast day and night.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V16","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V16","tier":"tier2"},{"word":"phase","pos":"noun","ipa":"/feɪz/","definition":"one stage in a series of changes (the Moon's phases)","arabic":"طور / مرحلة","example":"The full moon is one phase of the Moon.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V17","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V17","tier":"tier2"}],"explanation":{"text":"Science texts often have **special words** printed in **bold**. You can find their meanings in the **glossary** – a mini dictionary at the end of the text or book.\n\nA glossary is in **ABC (alphabetical) order**. To find *orbit*, look at the **first letter** (o), then the **second letter** (r). Read the **definition**, then go back to the sentence and check that it makes sense.\n\nSome glossaries also show **how to say** the word and a **picture**. Use the glossary **while** you read – don't wait until the end!","examples":["Bold word in a text: *The Moon **orbits** the Earth.* → glossary: **orbit** – to travel around another object in space.","Bold word: *We saw a **crescent** moon.* → glossary: **crescent** – the thin, curved shape of the new moon.","ABC order: **astronaut, crescent, orbit, phase, planet, rocket, shadow** (a, c, o, p, p, r, s).","Second letter: **phase** before **planet** (h comes before l).","Second letter: **space** before **spin**? → s-**p**-**a** vs. s-**p**-**i**: look at the **third** letter: a before i, so **space**, then **spin**.","Check in the sentence: *The Earth **spins** once every day.* → turns around and around → makes sense!","**spin** vs. **orbit**: Earth **spins** (turns on itself) AND **orbits** (goes around the Sun).","**day** and **night**: When your side of Earth faces the Sun, it is **day**; when it faces away, it is **night**.","**light**: The Moon has no light of its own; it **reflects** the Sun's light."],"common_errors":["✗ Looking for *orbit* under 'a' in the glossary. → ✓ Look under **o** (the first letter). (Use **ABC order**.)","✗ planet before phase → ✓ phase before planet (Second letters: **h** comes before **l**.)","✗ Spin and orbit mean the same. → ✓ Spin = turn on itself; orbit = go around something. (Different movements.)","✗ The moon make its own light. → ✓ The Moon reflects light from the Sun. (The Moon does **not** make light.)","✗ the earth → ✓ the Earth / Earth (Use a capital **E** for the planet.)","✗ An astronaut travel to space. → ✓ An astronaut travels to space. (One astronaut → **travels**.)","✗ Skipping the glossary and guessing. → ✓ Check bold words in the glossary while you read. (The glossary is there to help!)"],"arabic":"النصوص العلمية فيها كلمات خاصة مطبوعة بخط غامق، ونجد معانيها في المسرد (glossary)، وهو قاموس صغير في آخر النص أو الكتاب.\n\nالمسرد مرتب أبجديًا: لإيجاد orbit انظر إلى الحرف الأول (o) ثم الثاني (r)، واقرأ التعريف، ثم ارجع إلى الجملة لتتأكد أن المعنى مناسب.\n\nspin تعني الدوران حول النفس، وorbit تعني الدوران حول جسم آخر؛ فالأرض تدور حول نفسها وتدور حول الشمس.\n\nاكتب Earth بحرف كبير عندما تقصد كوكب الأرض. والقمر لا يصنع ضوءه بل يعكس ضوء الشمس."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Look up! Adam is observing the night sky over the desert.","on_screen":"Earth and Sky","visual":"Adam with a small telescope on a dune under a starry sky."},{"time":"00:20–01:00","narration":"The Moon, the stars, planets – and our planet, Earth! The Earth spins, and the Moon orbits.","on_screen":"moon · stars · planet · Earth · spin · orbit","visual":"Earth spins like a top; the Moon travels in a dotted circle."},{"time":"01:00–01:30","narration":"Day and night, light and shadow, and a thin crescent moon.","on_screen":"day · night · light · shadow · crescent","visual":"A town turns from day to night; a crescent appears."},{"time":"01:30–01:55","narration":"Rockets carry astronauts into space!","on_screen":"space · rocket · astronaut","visual":"A rocket launches; an astronaut waves from a window."},{"time":"01:55–02:40","narration":"Bold word? Go to the glossary! It's in ABC order: astronaut, crescent, orbit, phase, planet…","on_screen":"Glossary = ABC order 🔤","visual":"A finger runs down a glossary page and stops at 'orbit'."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Observe, contrast and learn the Moon's phases!","on_screen":"observe · contrast · phase","visual":"Four moon phases appear in a row."}],"captions_ar":["انظر إلى الأعلى! آدم يرصد سماء الليل فوق الصحراء.","القمر والنجوم والكواكب… وكوكبنا الأرض! الأرض تدور حول نفسها، والقمر يدور حولها.","النهار والليل، والضوء والظل، وهلال رفيع.","الصواريخ تحمل رواد الفضاء إلى الفضاء!","كلمة غامقة؟ اذهب إلى المسرد! إنه مرتب أبجديًا.","ارصد وقارن وتعلّم أطوار القمر!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, cheerful female teacher, speed 0.90. Adam: amazed researcher voice."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","instructions_ar":"اختر الكلمة الصحيحة.","items":[{"q":"The planet we live on is ___.","answer":"Earth","explanation":"Our planet.","explanation_ar":"الأرض.","options":["Earth","the Moon","a star","a rocket"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A person who travels into space is an ___.","answer":"astronaut","explanation":"Astronaut.","explanation_ar":"رائد فضاء.","options":["orbit","planet","observer only","astronaut"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A vehicle that flies into space is a ___.","answer":"rocket","explanation":"Rocket.","explanation_ar":"صاروخ.","options":["crescent","rocket","shadow","phase"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"The thin, curved shape of the new moon is a ___.","answer":"crescent","explanation":"Crescent.","explanation_ar":"هلال.","options":["planet","rocket","crescent","shadow"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A dark shape made when something blocks light is a ___.","answer":"shadow","explanation":"Shadow.","explanation_ar":"ظل.","options":["shadow","star","space","phase"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Huge balls of burning gas that we see at night are ___.","answer":"stars","explanation":"Stars.","explanation_ar":"النجوم.","options":["planets","moons","rockets","stars"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS1-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Use the glossary. Choose.","instructions_ar":"استخدم المسرد: اختر.","items":[{"q":"In a space glossary, which of these words comes FIRST?","answer":"astronaut","explanation":"a comes first.","explanation_ar":"astronaut.","options":["orbit","astronaut","rocket","shadow"],"dok":1,"skill":"ABC order","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which comes first in ABC order: *phase* or *planet*?","answer":"phase","explanation":"h before l.","explanation_ar":"phase.","options":["planet","They are the same.","Neither","phase"],"dok":2,"skill":"ABC order","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which comes first in ABC order: *space* or *spin*?","answer":"space","explanation":"Third letter: a before i.","explanation_ar":"space.","options":["space","spin","They are the same.","Neither"],"dok":2,"skill":"ABC order","stage":"guided"},{"q":"*The Moon **orbits** the Earth.* Glossary: *orbit – to travel around another object in space.* What does the Moon do?","answer":"travels around the Earth","explanation":"Use the definition.","explanation_ar":"يدور حول الأرض.","options":["turns into a star","makes its own light","travels around the Earth","stays still"],"dok":1,"skill":"glossary","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What is the difference between *spin* and *orbit*?","answer":"Spin is turning on itself; orbit is going around something else.","explanation":"Two movements.","explanation_ar":"spin حول النفس، orbit حول جسم آخر.","options":["They mean the same.","Spin is for rockets; orbit is for people.","Spin is turning on itself; orbit is going around something else.","Orbit is turning on itself."],"dok":2,"skill":"science words","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Where is the glossary usually found?","answer":"at the end of the text or book","explanation":"Glossary = end.","explanation_ar":"في النهاية.","options":["on the cover","at the end of the text or book","in the middle of a sentence","under every picture"],"dok":1,"skill":"text features","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS1-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"Let's ________ the night sky with binoculars.","answer":"observe","explanation":"Watch carefully.","explanation_ar":"نرصد.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The full moon is one ________ of the Moon.","answer":"phase","explanation":"One stage of change.","explanation_ar":"طور.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"In this lesson, we will ________ day and night to show how they are different.","answer":"contrast","explanation":"Show differences.","explanation_ar":"نقارن بالتباين.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The Earth ________s once every 24 hours.","answer":"spin","explanation":"Turns around and around.","explanation_ar":"يدور حول نفسه.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The Moon has no ________ of its own.","answer":"light","explanation":"What makes it possible to see.","explanation_ar":"ضوء.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Mars is a red ________.","answer":"planet","explanation":"A big round object that moves around the Sun.","explanation_ar":"كوكب.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS1-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write with the new words.","instructions_ar":"اكتب باستخدام الكلمات الجديدة.","items":[{"q":"Explain day and night using *spin*.","answer":"The Earth spins. When our side faces the Sun, it is day; when it faces away, it is night.","explanation":"spin + day/night.","explanation_ar":"spin + ليل/نهار.","dok":2,"skill":"explain","stage":"production"},{"q":"Put these words in ABC order: *star, moon, crescent, Earth, rocket*.","answer":"crescent, Earth, moon, rocket, star","explanation":"ABC order.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب أبجدي.","dok":2,"skill":"ABC order","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a glossary entry for *astronaut*.","answer":"astronaut – a person who travels into space.","explanation":"Word – definition.","explanation_ar":"كلمة – تعريف.","dok":2,"skill":"glossary","stage":"production"},{"q":"Would you like to observe the stars in the desert? Why?","answer":"Yes, because there are no city lights, so I can see many more stars.","explanation":"Opinion + because.","explanation_ar":"رأي + because.","dok":3,"skill":"opinion","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Glossary Rocket Race","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Glossary launch: a definition appears; the child scrolls an alphabetical glossary to find the word as fast as possible. Each correct word moves the rocket closer to space.","The teacher reads a definition card.","Teams race to find the word in their glossary.","The first team to point to the word and read its definition moves its rocket one step.","A team that reads the wrong word stays still.","The first rocket to reach space wins."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"A glossary is ___.","answer":"a mini dictionary of important words in a text","explanation":"Glossary = word meanings.","explanation_ar":"قاموس صغير.","options":["a list of chapters","a picture caption","a mini dictionary of important words in a text","a kind of telescope"],"dok":1,"skill":"text features"},{"q":"Words in a glossary are in ___ order.","answer":"ABC","explanation":"Alphabetical.","explanation_ar":"أبجدي.","options":["size","ABC","color","time"],"dok":1,"skill":"ABC order"},{"q":"*Observe the Moon every night.* *Observe* means ___.","answer":"watch carefully","explanation":"Observe = watch carefully.","explanation_ar":"ارصد.","options":["watch carefully","sleep","draw","throw"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"What does the Earth do once every 24 hours?","answer":"spins once","explanation":"One spin = one day.","explanation_ar":"يدور حول نفسه مرة.","options":["orbits the Moon","spins once","becomes a crescent","stops"],"dok":1,"skill":"science words"},{"q":"Which word comes LAST in ABC order?","answer":"star","explanation":"s is last.","explanation_ar":"star.","options":["rocket","planet","orbit","star"],"dok":2,"skill":"ABC order"},{"q":"Which sentence about the Moon's trip is correct?","answer":"The Moon orbits the Earth.","explanation":"One Moon → orbits.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The Moon orbit the Earth.","The Moon orbiting the Earth.","The Moon orbits the Earth.","The Moons orbits the Earth."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why is it night in Taif when it is day in New York?","answer":"Taif's side of Earth faces away from the Sun.","explanation":"Earth spins.","explanation_ar":"جانب الطائف بعيد عن الشمس.","options":["The Sun turns off.","Taif's side of Earth faces away from the Sun.","The Moon covers the Sun.","Taif has no Sun."],"dok":3,"skill":"explain"},{"q":"Which pair shows a CONTRAST?","answer":"Day is bright, but night is dark.","explanation":"but shows a difference.","explanation_ar":"تباين.","options":["Day is bright, and the Sun is bright.","Stars shine, and the Moon shines.","Day is bright, but night is dark.","Rockets fly, and planes fly."],"dok":2,"skill":"contrast"},{"q":"Why do science books have glossaries?","answer":"to help readers understand special science words","explanation":"Glossary helps.","explanation_ar":"لمساعدة القارئ على فهم الكلمات العلمية.","options":["to help readers understand special science words","to tell a story","to show the author's photo","to list the prices"],"dok":2,"skill":"author's purpose"},{"q":"*The Moon reflects the Sun's light.* Which glossary definition fits *reflects* here?","answer":"sends back light that hits it","explanation":"Reflect = send back light.","explanation_ar":"يعكس الضوء.","options":["makes its own fire","spins around fast","hides behind clouds","sends back light that hits it"],"dok":3,"skill":"glossary"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'moon': a full moon over the desert"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'stars': a starry night sky"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'planet': the planets around the Sun"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'Earth': a picture of Earth from space"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'orbit': a dotted circle path around Earth"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'day': a sunny town"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'night': a dark town with lights"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V08","prompt":"Picture for the word 'shadow': a child and a long shadow"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V09","prompt":"Picture for the word 'crescent': a thin crescent moon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V10","prompt":"Picture for the word 'space': dark space with stars and a planet"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V11","prompt":"Picture for the word 'rocket': a rocket launching with fire and smoke"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V12","prompt":"Picture for the word 'astronaut': an astronaut in a white space suit"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V13","prompt":"Picture for the word 'spin': a spinning top"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V14","prompt":"Picture for the word 'light': sunbeams shining on a ball"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V15","prompt":"Picture for the word 'observe': a child with binoculars looking at the sky"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V16","prompt":"Picture for the word 'contrast': a split picture: sun and moon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V17","prompt":"Picture for the word 'phase': four moon shapes in a row"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-01","prompt":"Children observe a crescent moon and stars over the desert."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-02","prompt":"Earth spinning and the Moon orbiting."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS1-03","prompt":"A glossary page with space words in ABC order."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V01","script":"moon. The moon is bright tonight."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V02","script":"stars. We saw many stars in the desert."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V03","script":"planet. Earth is a planet."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V04","script":"Earth. Earth has land and oceans."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V05","script":"orbit. The Moon orbits the Earth."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V06","script":"day. It is day when our side of Earth faces the Sun."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V07","script":"night. It is night when our side of Earth faces away from the Sun."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V08","script":"shadow. My shadow is long in the evening."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V09","script":"crescent. We saw the crescent moon at the start of Ramadan."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V10","script":"space. Astronauts travel to space."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V11","script":"rocket. The rocket roared into the sky."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V12","script":"astronaut. The astronaut floated in the space station."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V13","script":"spin. The Earth spins once every day."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V14","script":"light. The Moon reflects the Sun's light."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V15","script":"observe. Observe the Moon every night for a week."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V16","script":"contrast. Contrast day and night."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-V17","script":"phase. The full moon is one phase of the Moon."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Look up! Adam is observing the night sky over the desert. The Moon, the stars, planets – and our planet, Earth! The Earth spins, and the Moon orbits. Day and night, light and shadow, and a thin crescent moon. Rockets carry astronauts into space! Bold word? Go to the glossary! It's in ABC order: astronaut, crescent, orbit, phase, planet… Observe, contrast and learn the Moon's phases!"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2","title":"Why Does the Moon Change?","lesson_type":"close_reading","objectives":["read a science article of about 220 words and explain why the Moon seems to change","use a diagram and the words of the text together to understand the Moon's phases","answer literal, inferential and evaluative questions with evidence"],"objectives_ar":["قراءة مقال علمي من نحو 220 كلمة وشرح لماذا يبدو القمر متغيرًا.","استخدام الرسم التوضيحي وكلمات النص معًا لفهم أطوار القمر.","الإجابة عن أسئلة حرفية واستنتاجية وتقييمية مع الدليل."],"success_criteria":["I can explain why the Moon seems to change shape.","I can put the Moon's phases in order using the diagram.","I can use the glossary and the diagram as evidence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع شرح لماذا يبدو القمر متغير الشكل.","أستطيع ترتيب أطوار القمر باستخدام الرسم.","أستطيع استخدام المسرد والرسم دليلًا."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"notice","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˈnoʊtɪs/","definition":"to see or become aware of something","arabic":"يلاحظ","example":"Have you noticed the Moon's shape?","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"rock","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɑk/","definition":"the hard material that mountains are made of","arabic":"صخر","example":"The Moon is a big ball of rock.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"reflect","pos":"verb","ipa":"/rɪˈflɛkt/","definition":"to send back light that hits it","arabic":"يعكس","example":"A mirror reflects light.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"mirror","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmɪrər/","definition":"glass that shows a picture of what is in front of it","arabic":"مرآة","example":"Look in the mirror.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"amount","pos":"noun","ipa":"/əˈmaʊnt/","definition":"how much of something there is","arabic":"كمية / مقدار","example":"We see different amounts of the sunny side.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"hardly","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˈhɑrdli/","definition":"almost not","arabic":"بالكاد","example":"We can hardly see the new moon.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"diagram","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈdaɪəɡræm/","definition":"a drawing with labels that explains how something works","arabic":"رسم توضيحي","example":"The diagram shows the Moon's phases.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Science articles often have a **diagram** – a drawing with **labels** and **arrows** that shows how something works.\n\nRead the **text and the diagram together**. The text **explains**; the diagram **shows**. Match the **bold words** in the text with the **labels** in the diagram.\n\nSteps: (1) Read the **title** of the diagram. (2) Follow the **arrows** (they show order or movement). (3) Read each **label**. (4) Find the same idea in the text. (5) Use both as **evidence** in your answer.","examples":["Text: **The Moon reflects the Sun's light.** → Diagram: arrows from the Sun to the Moon and from the Moon to Earth.","Text: **The Moon orbits the Earth.** → Diagram: a dotted circle around Earth with the Moon in different places.","Label 1: **new moon** – the dark side faces us; we can hardly see it.","Label 2: **crescent** – a thin, curved shape (a few days after the new moon).","Label 3: **half moon** – half of the circle is bright (about one week later).","Label 4: **full moon** – the whole bright circle (about two weeks after the new moon).","Order (follow the arrows): **new moon → crescent → half moon → full moon → thinner again**.","Evidence from both: **The text says it takes about one month, and the diagram shows the full circle of phases.**","Real life: **The Islamic month begins with the new crescent moon** – for example, the start of Ramadan."],"common_errors":["✗ The Moon makes its own light. → ✓ The Moon reflects the Sun's light. (Check the text: **no light of its own**.)","✗ The Moon really changes its shape. → ✓ The Moon does not change; we see different amounts of its sunny side. (It only **looks** different.)","✗ Reading only the text and skipping the diagram. → ✓ Read the text **and** the diagram together. (The diagram shows what the text explains.)","✗ full moon → crescent → new moon (as the first steps) → ✓ new moon → crescent → half moon → full moon (Follow the **arrows** from the new moon.)","✗ The Moon orbit the Earth in one day. → ✓ The Moon orbits the Earth in about one month. (Check the number: **about one month**.)","✗ We can hard see the new moon. → ✓ We can hardly see the new moon. (hardly = almost not.)"],"arabic":"كثيرًا ما تحتوي المقالات العلمية على رسم توضيحي فيه تسميات وأسهم يُظهر كيف يعمل الشيء.\n\nاقرأ النص والرسم معًا: النص يشرح والرسم يُظهر، وطابق الكلمات الغامقة في النص مع التسميات في الرسم.\n\nالخطوات: اقرأ عنوان الرسم، واتبع الأسهم، واقرأ التسميات، وابحث عن الفكرة نفسها في النص، واستخدمهما معًا دليلًا.\n\nالقمر لا يصنع ضوءه بل يعكس ضوء الشمس، ولا يتغير شكله حقًا بل نرى أجزاء مختلفة من جانبه المضيء."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Adam drew the Moon every night. Why does it look different?","on_screen":"Why Does the Moon Change? 🌙","visual":"Adam's Moon Diary pages flip: crescent, half, full."},{"time":"00:20–01:35","narration":"Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night?…","on_screen":"(article, section by section)","visual":"Animation: the Sun lights half of the Moon; the Moon orbits Earth; the view from Earth changes."},{"time":"01:35–02:15","narration":"Read the text AND the diagram! Follow the arrows: new moon, crescent, half moon, full moon.","on_screen":"Text + diagram 🔍","visual":"A labelled diagram builds itself as the narrator reads."},{"time":"02:15–02:40","narration":"The Moon has no light. It reflects the Sun's light – like a mirror!","on_screen":"reflect = send back light","visual":"A flashlight shines on a ball and a mirror."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"The new crescent starts each month of the Islamic calendar – like the start of Ramadan!","on_screen":"The Moon and our calendar","visual":"Families look at a thin crescent over a mosque."}],"captions_ar":["رسم آدم القمر كل ليلة. لماذا يبدو مختلفًا؟","هل لاحظت يومًا أن القمر يبدو مختلفًا من ليلة إلى أخرى؟","اقرأ النص والرسم معًا! اتبع الأسهم: المحاق، الهلال، التربيع، البدر.","القمر لا ضوء له؛ إنه يعكس ضوء الشمس كالمرآة!","الهلال الجديد يبدأ كل شهر في التقويم الهجري، مثل بداية رمضان!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Adam observes the Moon over two weeks."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Why Does the Moon Change?","body":"Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night? Sometimes it is a thin crescent. Sometimes it is a big, bright circle. But the Moon does not really change its shape!\n\n**The Moon Has No Light**\n\nThe Moon does not make its own light. It is a big ball of rock. The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon **reflects** that light back to us, like a mirror.\n\n**The Moon's Trip Around Earth**\n\nThe Moon orbits the Earth. One trip takes about one month. As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunny side. These different shapes are called **phases**.\n\n**The Phases**\n\nAt the **new moon**, the sunny side faces away from us, so we can hardly see the Moon at all. A few days later, we see a thin crescent. Then we see a half moon. About two weeks after the new moon, the whole sunny side faces us, and we see a **full moon**. After that, the Moon slowly gets thinner again.\n\n**The Moon and Our Calendar**\n\nFor hundreds of years, people have used the Moon to count months. The Islamic calendar begins each month when people see the new crescent moon.","word_count":200,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS2-1","genre":"informational","role":"main","difficulty":"350L–500L","glossary":[{"word":"reflect","definition":"to send back light that hits it, like a mirror","arabic":"يعكس"},{"word":"phase","definition":"one shape the Moon seems to have during its trip around Earth","arabic":"طور القمر"},{"word":"new moon","definition":"the phase when we can hardly see the Moon","arabic":"المحاق"},{"word":"full moon","definition":"the phase when we see the whole bright circle","arabic":"البدر"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read the article. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ المقال واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is the Moon made of?","answer":"rock","explanation":"The Moon Has No Light.","explanation_ar":"صخر.","options":["fire","water","rock","gas"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where does the Moon's light come from?","answer":"the Sun","explanation":"It reflects the Sun's light.","explanation_ar":"الشمس.","options":["the Moon itself","the stars","the Earth's lamps","the Sun"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How long does one trip of the Moon around Earth take?","answer":"about one month","explanation":"The Moon's Trip Around Earth.","explanation_ar":"نحو شهر.","options":["one day","one year","one hour","about one month"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What are the different shapes of the Moon called?","answer":"phases","explanation":"Text: called phases.","explanation_ar":"أطوار.","options":["phases","planets","orbits","shadows"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"About how long after the new moon do we see a full moon?","answer":"about two weeks","explanation":"The Phases.","explanation_ar":"نحو أسبوعين.","options":["about two weeks","about two days","about two months","about two hours"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"When does each month of the Islamic calendar begin?","answer":"when people see the new crescent moon","explanation":"The Moon and Our Calendar.","explanation_ar":"برؤية الهلال.","options":["when the full moon appears","when people see the new crescent moon","when the Sun sets","on the first Monday"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Text and diagram. Choose.","instructions_ar":"النص والرسم: اختر.","items":[{"q":"Which phase comes right AFTER the new moon?","answer":"crescent","explanation":"Follow the arrows.","explanation_ar":"الهلال.","options":["full moon","half moon","another new moon","crescent"],"dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why can we hardly see the new moon?","answer":"Its sunny side faces away from us.","explanation":"The Phases.","explanation_ar":"جانبه المضيء بعيد عنا.","options":["It is very small.","Its sunny side faces away from us.","It has no rock.","Clouds always cover it."],"dok":2,"skill":"cause and effect","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Why does the Moon SEEM to change shape?","answer":"We see different amounts of its sunny side as it orbits.","explanation":"The Moon's Trip Around Earth.","explanation_ar":"نرى أجزاء مختلفة من جانبه المضيء.","options":["It grows and shrinks.","We see different amounts of its sunny side as it orbits.","Someone paints it.","It turns into a star."],"dok":2,"skill":"explain","stage":"guided"},{"q":"What does the writer compare the Moon to?","answer":"a mirror","explanation":"like a mirror.","explanation_ar":"مرآة.","options":["a lamp","a ball of fire","a mirror","a rocket"],"dok":1,"skill":"comparison","stage":"guided"},{"q":"In the diagram, what do the arrows from the Sun to the Moon show?","answer":"sunlight shining on the Moon","explanation":"Arrows show light.","explanation_ar":"ضوء الشمس.","options":["sunlight shining on the Moon","the Moon's shadow","a rocket's path","the Earth spinning"],"dok":2,"skill":"diagram","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which TWO features help you understand *phases*?","answer":"the bold word with the glossary and the diagram labels","explanation":"Bold word + glossary + diagram.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الغامقة والمسرد والرسم.","options":["the title and the page number","the first word and the last word","the bold word with the glossary and the diagram labels","a quote and a question"],"dok":3,"skill":"text features","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2-A3","type":"highlight","stage":"freer","instructions":"Find the evidence: Find the evidence.","instructions_ar":"ابحث عن الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Underline the sentence that says the Moon does not really change its shape.","answer":"But the Moon does not really change its shape!","explanation":"The writer says it directly.","explanation_ar":"يقولها الكاتب مباشرة.","evidence":"But the Moon does not really change its shape!","text_id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS2-1","dok":1,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night?","Sometimes it is a thin crescent.","Sometimes it is a big, bright circle.","But the Moon does not really change its shape!","**The Moon Has No Light**","The Moon does not make its own light.","It is a big ball of rock.","The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon **reflects** that light back to us, like a mirror.","**The Moon's Trip Around Earth**","The Moon orbits the Earth.","One trip takes about one month.","As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunny side.","These different shapes are called **phases**.","**The Phases**","At the **new moon**, the sunny side faces away from us, so we can hardly see the Moon at all.","A few days later, we see a thin crescent.","Then we see a half moon.","About two weeks after the new moon, the whole sunny side faces us, and we see a **full moon**.","After that, the Moon slowly gets thinner again.","**The Moon and Our Calendar**","For hundreds of years, people have used the Moon to count months.","The Islamic calendar begins each month when people see the new crescent moon."]},{"q":"Underline the sentence that explains where the Moon's light comes from.","answer":"The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon reflects that light back to us, like a mirror.","explanation":"Sun → Moon → us.","explanation_ar":"الشمس ← القمر ← نحن.","evidence":"The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon reflects that light back to us, like a mirror.","text_id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS2-1","dok":2,"skill":"evidence","stage":"freer","sentences":["Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night?","Sometimes it is a thin crescent.","Sometimes it is a big, bright circle.","But the Moon does not really change its shape!","**The Moon Has No Light**","The Moon does not make its own light.","It is a big ball of rock.","The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon **reflects** that light back to us, like a mirror.","**The Moon's Trip Around Earth**","The Moon orbits the Earth.","One trip takes about one month.","As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunny side.","These different shapes are called **phases**.","**The Phases**","At the **new moon**, the sunny side faces away from us, so we can hardly see the Moon at all.","A few days later, we see a thin crescent.","Then we see a half moon.","About two weeks after the new moon, the whole sunny side faces us, and we see a **full moon**.","After that, the Moon slowly gets thinner again.","**The Moon and Our Calendar**","For hundreds of years, people have used the Moon to count months.","The Islamic calendar begins each month when people see the new crescent moon."]},{"q":"Why does the writer end with the Islamic calendar?","answer":"to show how the Moon's phases matter in our lives","explanation":"It connects science to life.","explanation_ar":"ليُظهر أهمية أطوار القمر في حياتنا.","options":["to tell a story about Ramadan food","to persuade readers to buy calendars","to explain rockets","to show how the Moon's phases matter in our lives"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's purpose","stage":"freer"},{"q":"What is the main idea of *Why Does the Moon Change?*","answer":"The Moon seems to change because we see different amounts of its sunny side as it orbits Earth.","explanation":"It covers all sections.","explanation_ar":"يبدو القمر متغيرًا لأننا نرى أجزاء مختلفة من جانبه المضيء.","options":["The Moon seems to change because we see different amounts of its sunny side as it orbits Earth.","The Moon is made of rock.","Ramadan begins with a crescent.","The Sun is bright."],"dok":3,"skill":"main idea","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Explain with evidence.","instructions_ar":"اشرح مع الدليل.","items":[{"q":"Explain why the Moon shines at night. Use the word *reflects*.","answer":"The Moon shines because it reflects light from the Sun, like a mirror.","explanation":"Use reflects.","explanation_ar":"استخدم reflects.","dok":2,"skill":"explain","stage":"production"},{"q":"Put four phases in order, starting with the new moon.","answer":"new moon, crescent, half moon, full moon","explanation":"Four phases.","explanation_ar":"أربعة أطوار.","dok":1,"skill":"sequence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Use the text AND the diagram to explain the full moon.","answer":"The text says the whole sunny side faces us, and the diagram shows the Moon on the far side of Earth from the Sun, so we see a full bright circle.","explanation":"Text + diagram.","explanation_ar":"النص + الرسم.","dok":3,"skill":"evidence","stage":"production"},{"q":"Why is the crescent moon important to Muslims?","answer":"It tells us when a new month begins, like Ramadan or Shawwal.","explanation":"Connect to life.","explanation_ar":"ربط بالحياة.","dok":2,"skill":"connect","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS2-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Why Does the Moon Change?\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Why Does the Moon Change?”.","answer":"200 words","title":"Why Does the Moon Change?","body":"Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night? Sometimes it is a thin crescent. Sometimes it is a big, bright circle. But the Moon does not really change its shape!\n\n**The Moon Has No Light**\n\nThe Moon does not make its own light. It is a big ball of rock. The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon **reflects** that light back to us, like a mirror.\n\n**The Moon's Trip Around Earth**\n\nThe Moon orbits the Earth. One trip takes about one month. As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunny side. These different shapes are called **phases**.\n\n**The Phases**\n\nAt the **new moon**, the sunny side faces away from us, so we can hardly see the Moon at all. A few days later, we see a thin crescent. Then we see a half moon. About two weeks after the new moon, the whole sunny side faces us, and we see a **full moon**. After that, the Moon slowly gets thinner again.\n\n**The Moon and Our Calendar**\n\nFor hundreds of years, people have used the Moon to count months. The Islamic calendar begins each month when people see the new crescent moon.","words":200,"limit":186}],"time_limit_sec":186}],"game":{"name":"Phase Parade","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Moon cycle: phase cards orbit a picture of Earth; the child drags them into order around the circle and taps each to hear its name. A complete cycle makes the Moon glow full.","Teams get mixed phase cards.","They line them up in order starting with the new moon.","Each player explains one phase using 'sunny side'.","Teams check with the lamp-and-ball model.","Correct order + explanations = 3 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What is *Why Does the Moon Change?* mostly about?","answer":"why the Moon seems to change shape","explanation":"The title and sections.","explanation_ar":"لماذا يبدو القمر متغيرًا.","options":["how rockets fly","why the Moon seems to change shape","how to make a calendar","stars in the desert"],"dok":1,"skill":"main topic"},{"q":"The Moon ___ the Sun's light.","answer":"reflects","explanation":"Reflects.","explanation_ar":"يعكس.","options":["makes","eats","hides","reflects"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"A drawing with labels that explains how something works is a ___.","answer":"diagram","explanation":"Diagram.","explanation_ar":"رسم توضيحي.","options":["diagram","caption","glossary","heading"],"dok":1,"skill":"text features"},{"q":"*We can hardly see the new moon.* *Hardly* means ___.","answer":"almost not","explanation":"Hardly = almost not.","explanation_ar":"بالكاد.","options":["very well","quickly","almost not","always"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"Which phase shows the whole bright circle?","answer":"full moon","explanation":"Full moon.","explanation_ar":"البدر.","options":["new moon","full moon","crescent","half moon"],"dok":1,"skill":"phases"},{"q":"Which sentence about the Moon's light is correct?","answer":"The Moon does not make its own light.","explanation":"does not + base verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["The Moon do not make its own light.","The Moon don't makes its light.","The Moon not make light.","The Moon does not make its own light."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which order is correct?","answer":"new moon → crescent → half moon → full moon","explanation":"Follow the cycle.","explanation_ar":"الترتيب الصحيح.","options":["new moon → crescent → half moon → full moon","full moon → new moon → half moon → crescent","crescent → full moon → new moon → half moon","half moon → crescent → full moon → new moon"],"dok":2,"skill":"sequence"},{"q":"Why does reading the diagram help?","answer":"It shows the Moon's positions that the text explains.","explanation":"Text + diagram work together.","explanation_ar":"يُظهر ما يشرحه النص.","options":["It replaces the whole text.","It tells a story.","It is only decoration.","It shows the Moon's positions that the text explains."],"dok":2,"skill":"diagram"},{"q":"If you see a full moon tonight, about how long until the next full moon?","answer":"about one month","explanation":"One orbit ≈ one month.","explanation_ar":"نحو شهر.","options":["about one month","one night","one week","one year"],"dok":3,"skill":"apply"},{"q":"What would happen if the Sun did not shine on the Moon?","answer":"We could not see the Moon.","explanation":"No light to reflect.","explanation_ar":"لن نرى القمر.","options":["The Moon would be brighter.","The Moon would turn into a star.","We could not see the Moon.","Nothing would change."],"dok":3,"skill":"reasoning"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'notice': a child pointing up at the sky"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'rock': a gray rock"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'reflect': a mirror bouncing a beam of light"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'mirror': a round mirror reflecting a lamp"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'amount': three glasses with different amounts of water"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'hardly': a very faint moon shape in a dark sky"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'diagram': a labelled science drawing"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-01","prompt":"A labelled diagram of the Moon's phases around Earth."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-02","prompt":"Light shining on a ball and bouncing to a child's eyes."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS2-03","prompt":"A family looks at the new crescent moon above a mosque."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V01","script":"notice. Have you noticed the Moon's shape?"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V02","script":"rock. The Moon is a big ball of rock."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V03","script":"reflect. A mirror reflects light."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V04","script":"mirror. Look in the mirror."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V05","script":"amount. We see different amounts of the sunny side."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V06","script":"hardly. We can hardly see the new moon."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-V07","script":"diagram. The diagram shows the Moon's phases."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-T1","script":"Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night? Sometimes it is a thin crescent. Sometimes it is a big, bright circle. But the Moon does not really change its shape! **The Moon Has No Light** The Moon does not make its own light. It is a big ball of rock. The Sun shines on the Moon, and the Moon **reflects** that light back to us, like a mirror. **The Moon's Trip Around Earth** The Moon orbits the Earth. One trip takes about one month. As it moves, we see different amounts of its sunny side. These different shapes are called **phases**. **The Phases** At the **new moon**, the sunny side faces away from us, so we can hardly see the Moon at all. A few days later, we see a thin crescent. Then we see a half moon. About two weeks after the new moon, the whole sunny side faces us, and we see a **full moon**. After that, the Moon slowly gets thinner again. **The Moon and Our Calendar** For hundreds of years, people have used the Moon to count months. The Islamic calendar begins each month when people see the new crescent moon."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Adam drew the Moon every night. Why does it look different? Have you ever noticed that the Moon looks different from night to night?… Read the text AND the diagram! Follow the arrows: new moon, crescent, half moon, full moon. The Moon has no light. It reflects the Sun's light – like a mirror! The new crescent starts each month of the Islamic calendar – like the start of Ramadan!"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3","title":"Compare and contrast two texts: \"Day or Night: Which Is Better?\"","lesson_type":"strategy_paired_text","objectives":["compare and contrast two texts on the same topic: what is the same and what is different","contrast the purpose, structure and language of an informational text and an opinion text","complete a Venn diagram and write compare/contrast sentences with both, but and however"],"objectives_ar":["المقارنة بين نصين في الموضوع نفسه: أوجه التشابه والاختلاف.","مقارنة الغرض والبنية واللغة في نص معلوماتي ونص رأي.","إكمال مخطط فن وكتابة جمل مقارنة بـ both وbut وhowever."],"success_criteria":["I can find two things that are the same in both texts.","I can find two differences (purpose, features or details).","I can write a compare sentence and a contrast sentence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع إيجاد شيئين متشابهين في النصين.","أستطيع إيجاد اختلافين (الغرض أو الخصائص أو التفاصيل).","أستطيع كتابة جملة تشابه وجملة اختلاف."],"map_area":"Informational Text: Key Ideas and Details","vocabulary":[{"word":"silver","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɪlvər/","definition":"a shiny gray-white color","arabic":"فضي","example":"The silver Moon shone over the desert.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"peaceful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈpisfəl/","definition":"calm and quiet","arabic":"هادئ / مريح","example":"The desert at night is peaceful.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"starry","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈstɑri/","definition":"full of stars","arabic":"مرصّع بالنجوم","example":"We slept under a starry sky.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"sunshine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌnʃaɪn/","definition":"the light and heat from the Sun","arabic":"ضوء الشمس / إشراقها","example":"Plants need sunshine to grow.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"however","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/haʊˈɛvər/","definition":"a word that shows a different idea (like but)","arabic":"ومع ذلك / لكن","example":"The day is bright. However, it is very hot.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"both","pos":"determiner","ipa":"/boʊθ/","definition":"the two together","arabic":"كلا / كلاهما","example":"Both texts talk about the Moon.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"similar","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈsɪmələr/","definition":"almost the same","arabic":"متشابه","example":"The two texts are similar in some ways.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"To **compare** is to find what is the **same**. To **contrast** is to find what is **different**. We can compare and contrast two texts on the **same topic**.\n\nLook at four things: (1) **Topic** – what is each text about? (2) **Purpose** – inform, persuade or entertain? (3) **Features** – headings, glossary, diagrams OR opinion words like *I think*, reasons, *That is why*. (4) **Details** – what facts or ideas are in each?\n\nUse a **Venn diagram**: differences in the outer circles, things that are the same in the middle. Signal words: **both, also, similar** (same) and **but, however, different** (different).","examples":["Same topic: **Both texts are about the night sky and the Moon.**","Same detail: **Both texts mention the phases of the Moon.**","Different purpose: **The article informs, but Layla's text gives her opinion.**","Different features: **The article has headings and a glossary. However, Layla's text has reasons with First and Second.**","Different language: **The article uses facts (about one month). Layla uses opinion words (I think, nothing is more peaceful).**","Only in the article: **The Moon reflects the Sun's light.**","Only in Layla's text: **Families sit outside and drink tea under the stars.**","Layla's counterpoint: **Of course, the day has sunshine…** – she admits the other side, then answers it.","Compare frame: *Both texts…* · Contrast frame: *The article…, but Layla's text…* / *However, …*"],"common_errors":["✗ Listing only things that are the same. → ✓ Give **similarities and differences**. (Compare AND contrast.)","✗ Both text are about the Moon. → ✓ Both texts are about the Moon. (Both + **texts** (plural).)","✗ However the night is cool. → ✓ However, the night is cool. (Comma after **However** at the start.)","✗ The article says night is better. → ✓ Layla says night is better; the article gives facts only. (Check **which text** says what.)","✗ Layla's text informs with headings. → ✓ Layla's text gives an opinion with reasons. (Different purposes and features.)","✗ The article is similar with Layla's text. → ✓ The article is similar to Layla's text. (similar **to**.)"],"arabic":"المقارنة تعني إيجاد المتشابه، والمقابلة (contrast) تعني إيجاد المختلف، ونطبقهما على نصين في الموضوع نفسه.\n\nانظر إلى أربعة أمور: الموضوع، والغرض (إعلام/إقناع/إمتاع)، والخصائص (عناوين ومسرد ورسم أو كلمات رأي وأسباب)، والتفاصيل.\n\nاستخدم مخطط فن: المختلف في الدائرتين الخارجيتين، والمتشابه في الوسط. كلمات التشابه: both, also, similar، وكلمات الاختلاف: but, however, different.\n\nضع فاصلة بعد However في بداية الجملة، وقل similar to."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Two texts about the sky! One gives facts, one gives an opinion. Let's compare and contrast!","on_screen":"Compare 🤝 Contrast ↔️","visual":"Two books open side by side under a night sky."},{"time":"00:20–01:20","narration":"Day or Night: Which Is Better? by Layla. Some people love the bright day, but I think night is better…","on_screen":"(opinion text)","visual":"Layla draws moon phases on a dune; her family drinks tea under the stars."},{"time":"01:20–01:55","narration":"Same: both talk about the Moon and its phases.","on_screen":"Both ✔","visual":"Two circles overlap; 'Moon phases' drops into the middle."},{"time":"01:55–02:35","narration":"Different: the article informs with headings and a glossary; Layla persuades with reasons and 'I think'.","on_screen":"Different purposes & features","visual":"Labels fly into the outer circles: headings, glossary / I think, reasons."},{"time":"02:35–03:00","narration":"Use both, also, but and however to write about two texts!","on_screen":"both · also · but · however","visual":"Signal words click into sentence frames."}],"captions_ar":["نصان عن السماء! أحدهما يقدم حقائق والآخر رأيًا. لنقارن بينهما!","النهار أم الليل: أيهما أفضل؟ بقلم ليلى. بعض الناس يحبون النهار المشرق، لكنني أظن أن الليل أفضل…","المتشابه: كلاهما يتحدث عن القمر وأطواره.","المختلف: المقال يُعلِم بالعناوين والمسرد، وليلى تُقنع بالأسباب وI think.","استخدم both وalso وbut وhowever للكتابة عن نصين!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Layla reads her opinion text dreamily."},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Day or Night: Which Is Better?","body":"by Layla\n\nSome people love the bright day, but I think night is better. Here are my reasons.\n\nFirst, the night sky is beautiful. In the desert, you can see thousands of stars and the silver Moon. I love to draw the different phases of the Moon in my notebook.\n\nSecond, the night is cool and quiet. In summer, the day is very hot, but at night we can sit outside with our family and drink tea under the stars.\n\nOf course, the day has sunshine, and we need it to play and to grow plants. But for me, nothing is more peaceful than a starry night.\n\nThat is why I think night is better than day!","word_count":117,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS3-1","genre":"opinion/argument","role":"paired","difficulty":"350L–500L","glossary":[{"word":"silver","definition":"a shiny gray-white color","arabic":"فضي"},{"word":"peaceful","definition":"calm and quiet","arabic":"هادئ ومريح"},{"word":"starry","definition":"full of stars","arabic":"مرصّع بالنجوم"}]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read *Day or Night: Which Is Better?*. Choose the answer.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ نص الرأي واختر الإجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is Layla's opinion?","answer":"Night is better than day.","explanation":"First paragraph.","explanation_ar":"الليل أفضل من النهار.","options":["Day is better than night.","Night is better than day.","Both are boring.","The Moon is too small."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","text_id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS3-1","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is Layla's FIRST reason?","answer":"The night sky is beautiful.","explanation":"First, …","explanation_ar":"سماء الليل جميلة.","options":["The night is cool and quiet.","The night sky is beautiful.","The day has sunshine.","Plants need the Sun."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What is Layla's SECOND reason?","answer":"The night is cool and quiet.","explanation":"Second, …","explanation_ar":"الليل بارد وهادئ.","options":["The night is cool and quiet.","The night sky is beautiful.","She can draw in the day.","The day is long."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does Layla's family do at night in summer?","answer":"sit outside and drink tea under the stars","explanation":"Paragraph 3.","explanation_ar":"يجلسون في الخارج ويشربون الشاي.","options":["go to school","sleep on the beach","sit outside and drink tea under the stars","fly a kite"],"dok":1,"skill":"key details","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does Layla agree is good about the day?","answer":"It has sunshine that we need to play and grow plants.","explanation":"Of course, …","explanation_ar":"ضوء الشمس.","options":["It is cool and quiet.","It has many stars.","It has a silver Moon.","It has sunshine that we need to play and grow plants."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterpoint","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"How does Layla end her text?","answer":"That is why I think night is better than day!","explanation":"Last sentence.","explanation_ar":"That is why…","options":["First, the night sky is beautiful.","Some people love the bright day.","That is why I think night is better than day!","The Moon reflects light."],"dok":1,"skill":"closing","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-A2","type":"mcq","stage":"guided","instructions":"Guided practice: Compare and contrast. Choose.","instructions_ar":"قارن وقابل: اختر.","items":[{"q":"What topic do BOTH texts talk about?","answer":"the Moon and the night sky","explanation":"Both mention the Moon.","explanation_ar":"القمر وسماء الليل.","options":["rockets","the Moon and the night sky","the human heart","camels"],"dok":1,"skill":"compare","stage":"guided"},{"q":"How are the PURPOSES different?","answer":"The article informs; Layla's text gives an opinion.","explanation":"Facts vs. opinion.","explanation_ar":"الإعلام مقابل الرأي.","options":["Both entertain.","Both persuade you to buy something.","The article gives an opinion; Layla informs.","The article informs; Layla's text gives an opinion."],"dok":2,"skill":"contrast purpose","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which feature is ONLY in the article?","answer":"a glossary and headings","explanation":"Text features.","explanation_ar":"المسرد والعناوين.","options":["a glossary and headings","the word 'I think'","reasons with First and Second","family tea"],"dok":2,"skill":"contrast features","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which detail is ONLY in Layla's text?","answer":"Families drink tea under the stars.","explanation":"Only Layla mentions tea.","explanation_ar":"الشاي تحت النجوم.","options":["Families drink tea under the stars.","The Moon reflects the Sun's light.","One trip around Earth takes about a month.","The Islamic month begins with the crescent."],"dok":2,"skill":"contrast details","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which detail is in BOTH the Moon article and Layla's text?","answer":"the phases of the Moon","explanation":"Both mention phases.","explanation_ar":"أطوار القمر.","options":["the Islamic calendar","drinking tea","the phases of the Moon","the Moon is made of rock"],"dok":2,"skill":"compare details","stage":"guided"},{"q":"Which sentence CONTRASTS the two texts correctly?","answer":"The article uses facts, but Layla's text uses opinion words.","explanation":"but shows a difference.","explanation_ar":"جملة اختلاف.","options":["Both texts are about the Moon.","The two texts are similar.","The article uses facts, but Layla's text uses opinion words.","Both texts mention phases."],"dok":2,"skill":"contrast sentences","stage":"guided"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Complete the Venn diagram.","instructions_ar":"أكمل مخطط فن.","items":[{"q":"Article only: write two details or features.","answer":"It has a glossary and headings. It says the Moon reflects the Sun's light.","explanation":"Two items.","explanation_ar":"عنصران.","dok":2,"skill":"contrast","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Layla's text only: write two details or features.","answer":"It uses 'I think' and gives reasons. It talks about drinking tea under the stars.","explanation":"Two items.","explanation_ar":"عنصران.","dok":2,"skill":"contrast","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Both: write two things.","answer":"Both are about the night sky. Both mention the phases of the Moon.","explanation":"Two items.","explanation_ar":"عنصران.","dok":2,"skill":"compare","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Write one sentence with *However*.","answer":"The article teaches facts. However, Layla's text shares her feelings and opinion.","explanation":"However + comma.","explanation_ar":"However + فاصلة.","dok":3,"skill":"contrast sentences","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Compare, contrast and give your view.","instructions_ar":"قارن وقابل وأبدِ رأيك.","items":[{"q":"Write a *both* sentence about the two texts.","answer":"Both texts talk about the Moon and its phases.","explanation":"Both + plural.","explanation_ar":"Both + جمع.","dok":2,"skill":"compare","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a *but* sentence about the two texts.","answer":"The article informs readers, but Layla's text tries to persuade them.","explanation":"…, but…","explanation_ar":"…, but…","dok":2,"skill":"contrast","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which text helped you learn more facts? Why?","answer":"The article, because it has facts, a diagram and a glossary.","explanation":"Evaluate + reason.","explanation_ar":"تقييم + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"evaluate","stage":"production"},{"q":"Do you agree with Layla? Give one reason.","answer":"No, I think day is better because I can play football in the sunshine.","explanation":"Opinion + reason.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب.","dok":3,"skill":"opinion","stage":"production"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-TR-1","type":"timed_reading","instructions":"Timed reading: Read \"Day or Night: Which Is Better?\" aloud or silently. Try to finish in the time.","instructions_ar":"اقرأ النص وحاول أن تنهيه في الوقت المحدد.","items":[{"q":"Read “Day or Night: Which Is Better?”.","answer":"117 words","title":"Day or Night: Which Is Better?","body":"by Layla\n\nSome people love the bright day, but I think night is better. Here are my reasons.\n\nFirst, the night sky is beautiful. In the desert, you can see thousands of stars and the silver Moon. I love to draw the different phases of the Moon in my notebook.\n\nSecond, the night is cool and quiet. In summer, the day is very hot, but at night we can sit outside with our family and drink tea under the stars.\n\nOf course, the day has sunshine, and we need it to play and to grow plants. But for me, nothing is more peaceful than a starry night.\n\nThat is why I think night is better than day!","words":117,"limit":115}],"time_limit_sec":115},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS3-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"Venn Diagram","instructions":"Organizer: Write details only in the article on the left, details only in Layla's text on the right and things in both texts in the middle.","items":[{"q":"Article only (Why Does the Moon Change?)","answer":"facts with numbers (about one month); headings; a glossary and a diagram; the Moon reflects the Sun's light; purpose: inform"},{"q":"Both texts","answer":"the Moon; the phases of the Moon; the night sky"},{"q":"Layla's text only (Day or Night: Which Is Better?)","answer":"opinion words (I think, nothing is more peaceful); reasons with First and Second; family tea under the stars; purpose: persuade/give an opinion"}]}],"game":{"name":"Hoop Detectives","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Venn sort: strips float down; the child drags each into Article only, Layla only or Both. A full correct diagram lights up the night sky with stars.","Teams take turns drawing a strip.","The player places it in the left hoop, the right hoop or the middle.","The player must explain with evidence ('The article says…').","Other teams can challenge.","Correct place + evidence = 2 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"To *contrast* two texts means to find ___.","answer":"how they are different","explanation":"Contrast = differences.","explanation_ar":"أوجه الاختلاف.","options":["how they are the same","the title only","how they are different","the author's age"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Where do you write similarities in a Venn diagram?","answer":"in the middle","explanation":"Middle = both.","explanation_ar":"في الوسط.","options":["in the left circle only","in the right circle only","under the title","in the middle"],"dok":1,"skill":"organizer"},{"q":"Which signal word shows something is the SAME?","answer":"both","explanation":"both = same.","explanation_ar":"both.","options":["however","but","different","both"],"dok":1,"skill":"signal words"},{"q":"*Nothing is more peaceful than a starry night.* *Peaceful* means ___.","answer":"calm and quiet","explanation":"Peaceful = calm.","explanation_ar":"هادئ.","options":["calm and quiet","noisy and busy","very hot","very bright"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *However* correctly?","answer":"However, the day is very hot in summer.","explanation":"Comma after However.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["However the day, is very hot.","However, the day is very hot in summer.","The day however, is hot however.","However; the day is hot."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *similar* correctly?","answer":"Layla's text is similar to the article in one way.","explanation":"similar to.","explanation_ar":"similar to.","options":["Layla's text is similar with the article.","Layla's text is similar to the article in one way.","Layla's text similar the article.","Layla's text is similarly to the article."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Why does Layla write *Of course, the day has sunshine…*?","answer":"to show she understands the other side before giving her answer","explanation":"Counterpoint.","explanation_ar":"لتُظهر أنها تفهم الرأي الآخر.","options":["to show she understands the other side before giving her answer","to change her opinion","to give a fact about the Moon","to end the text"],"dok":3,"skill":"author's craft"},{"q":"Which text would be better for a science project about the Moon?","answer":"the article, because it has facts, a diagram and a glossary","explanation":"Facts are needed.","explanation_ar":"المقال.","options":["Layla's text, because it has opinions","neither text","the article, because it has facts, a diagram and a glossary","both are the same for a science project"],"dok":3,"skill":"evaluate"},{"q":"Which is a FACT from the texts?","answer":"The Moon orbits the Earth in about one month.","explanation":"Checkable fact.","explanation_ar":"حقيقة.","options":["Night is better than day.","The Moon orbits the Earth in about one month.","Nothing is more peaceful than a starry night.","I love to draw the Moon."],"dok":2,"skill":"fact vs. opinion"},{"q":"How are the STRUCTURES of the two texts different?","answer":"The article uses headings for each part; Layla uses an opinion, two reasons and a closing.","explanation":"Different structures.","explanation_ar":"بنيتان مختلفتان.","options":["Both use headings.","Both are plays.","Layla's text has a glossary.","The article uses headings for each part; Layla uses an opinion, two reasons and a closing."],"dok":3,"skill":"contrast structure"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'silver': a silver coin and a silver moon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'peaceful': a quiet desert camp at night"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'starry': a sky full of stars"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'sunshine': a sunny garden"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'however': a balance scale with two different sides"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'both': two hands holding one moon"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'similar': two similar pictures side by side"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-01","prompt":"Layla's family drinks tea under a starry sky while she draws the Moon."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-02","prompt":"A Venn diagram comparing the article and Layla's opinion."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS3-03","prompt":"A split picture of a sunny day and a starry night."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V01","script":"silver. The silver Moon shone over the desert."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V02","script":"peaceful. The desert at night is peaceful."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V03","script":"starry. We slept under a starry sky."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V04","script":"sunshine. Plants need sunshine to grow."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V05","script":"however. The day is bright. However, it is very hot."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V06","script":"both. Both texts talk about the Moon."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-V07","script":"similar. The two texts are similar in some ways."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-T1","script":"by Layla Some people love the bright day, but I think night is better. Here are my reasons. First, the night sky is beautiful. In the desert, you can see thousands of stars and the silver Moon. I love to draw the different phases of the Moon in my notebook. Second, the night is cool and quiet. In summer, the day is very hot, but at night we can sit outside with our family and drink tea under the stars. Of course, the day has sunshine, and we need it to play and to grow plants. But for me, nothing is more peaceful than a starry night. That is why I think night is better than day!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Two texts about the sky! One gives facts, one gives an opinion. Let's compare and contrast! Day or Night: Which Is Better? by Layla. Some people love the bright day, but I think night is better… Same: both talk about the Moon and its phases. Different: the article informs with headings and a glossary; Layla persuades with reasons and 'I think'. Use both, also, but and however to write about two texts!"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS4","title":"Writing Skill: Opinion + 2 reasons + closing","lesson_type":"writing_skill","objectives":["write an opinion paragraph with an opinion, two reasons with support and a closing (OREO)","support each reason with an example or a fact","use opinion words and reason starters (I believe…, My first reason is that…)"],"objectives_ar":["كتابة فقرة رأي فيها رأي وسببان مدعومان وخاتمة (OREO).","دعم كل سبب بمثال أو حقيقة.","استخدام كلمات الرأي وبدايات الأسباب."],"success_criteria":["I can state my opinion clearly in the first sentence.","I can give two reasons, each with an example or a fact.","I can restate my opinion in a closing sentence."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع ذكر رأيي بوضوح في الجملة الأولى.","أستطيع ذكر سببين مع مثال أو حقيقة لكل منهما.","أستطيع إعادة صياغة رأيي في جملة ختامية."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"believe","pos":"verb","ipa":"/bɪˈliv/","definition":"to think that something is true or right","arabic":"يعتقد / يؤمن","example":"I believe day is better.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"in my opinion","pos":"phrase","ipa":"/ɪn maɪ əˈpɪnjən/","definition":"words that show what you think","arabic":"في رأيي","example":"In my opinion, night is more peaceful.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"reason","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrizən/","definition":"why you think something","arabic":"سبب","example":"My first reason is that the day is full of action.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"action","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈækʃən/","definition":"doing things; being busy and active","arabic":"حركة / نشاط","example":"The day is full of action.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"sunlight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈsʌnlaɪt/","definition":"the light from the Sun","arabic":"ضوء الشمس","example":"Our bodies need sunlight.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"shade","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ʃeɪd/","definition":"a cool place out of the sun","arabic":"ظل","example":"Sit in the shade on hot days.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"OREO","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɔrioʊ/","definition":"a plan for opinion writing: Opinion, Reason, Example, Opinion again","arabic":"خطة OREO لكتابة الرأي","example":"Use OREO to plan your paragraph.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"An **opinion paragraph** tells what **you think** and **why**. Use the **OREO** plan: **O**pinion → **R**eason → **E**xample (or fact) → **O**pinion again.\n\nGive **two reasons**. Start each with a reason starter: **My first reason is that… / My second reason is that…** Support each reason with **For example, …** or a **fact**.\n\nStrong writers sometimes mention the **other side** (*Some people say…*) and answer it with **However, …**. End by saying your opinion again in **new words**: **For these reasons, … / That is why…**","examples":["Opinion: **I believe day is better than night.**","Opinion (other starters): **I think… / In my opinion, …**","Reason 1: **My first reason is that the day is full of action.**","Example: **For example, I can play football with my team in the park.**","Reason 2: **My second reason is that sunshine is good for us.**","Fact: **Our bodies need sunlight to make strong bones.**","Other side: **Some people say the night is cool and quiet.**","Answer: **However, I can sit in the shade and still enjoy the day.**","Closing: **For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!**"],"common_errors":["✗ Day is better. (no reasons) → ✓ I believe day is better because… My first reason is that… (Give **two reasons**.)","✗ My first reason is the day is fun. → ✓ My first reason is that the day is full of action. (Use **that** + a full idea.)","✗ A reason with no example. → ✓ …full of action. For example, I can play football. (Support each reason.)","✗ I am thinking day is better. → ✓ I think day is better. (Use **I think** (not I am thinking) for opinions.)","✗ In my opinion day is better. → ✓ In my opinion, day is better. (Comma after **In my opinion**.)","✗ Closing that changes the opinion: 'Night is nice too.' → ✓ For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time! (Keep the **same** opinion at the end.)"],"arabic":"فقرة الرأي تخبر بما تعتقده ولماذا. استخدم خطة OREO: الرأي ← السبب ← المثال أو الحقيقة ← الرأي مرة أخرى.\n\nاذكر سببين، وابدأ كلًّا منهما بـ My first reason is that… / My second reason is that…، وادعمه بـ For example أو بحقيقة.\n\nالكاتب الماهر قد يذكر الرأي الآخر (Some people say…) ثم يرد عليه بـ However.\n\nاختم بإعادة رأيك بكلمات جديدة: For these reasons… / That is why…، ولا تغيّر رأيك في النهاية."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Omar read Layla's opinion – and he does NOT agree! He writes his own.","on_screen":"Day Is Better! ☀️","visual":"Omar holds a football; Layla's text is pinned on the wall behind him."},{"time":"00:20–01:10","narration":"I read Layla's opinion, but I believe day is better than night. My first reason is that…","on_screen":"(model paragraph)","visual":"Each sentence appears in an OREO layer color."},{"time":"01:10–01:45","narration":"OREO: Opinion, Reason, Example, Opinion again!","on_screen":"O · R · E · O","visual":"A cookie stack builds with four labelled layers."},{"time":"01:45–02:25","narration":"Answer the other side: Some people say the night is cool. However, I can sit in the shade!","on_screen":"Some people say… However, …","visual":"A see-saw tips back toward Omar's opinion."},{"time":"02:25–03:00","narration":"End strong: For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!","on_screen":"Closing = opinion again","visual":"Omar kicks the ball; the word 'closing' lights up."}],"captions_ar":["قرأ عمر رأي ليلى ولم يوافق! فكتب رأيه.","قرأت رأي ليلى، لكنني أعتقد أن النهار أفضل من الليل. سببي الأول…","OREO: الرأي، السبب، المثال، الرأي مرة أخرى!","رُدّ على الرأي الآخر: يقول بعضهم إن الليل بارد، ومع ذلك أستطيع الجلوس في الظل!","اختم بقوة: لهذه الأسباب سيبقى النهار وقتي المفضل!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Omar reads his opinion with energy, like a sports commentator."},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Day Is Better! (by Omar)","body":"I read Layla's opinion, but I believe day is better than night. My first reason is that the day is full of action. For example, I can play football with my team in the park after school. My second reason is that sunshine is good for us. Our bodies need sunlight to make strong bones, and plants need it to grow food. Some people say the night is cool and quiet. However, I can sit in the shade and still enjoy the bright, busy day. For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!","word_count":96,"audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-T1","id":"TXT-RW-L03-U6-LS4-1","genre":"model text","role":"model","difficulty":"350L–500L","glossary":[],"annotations":["**O – Opinion:** *I believe day is better than night.* – the first sentence says what the writer thinks.","**R – Reason 1:** *My first reason is that the day is full of action.* **E – Example:** *For example, I can play football…*","**R – Reason 2:** *My second reason is that sunshine is good for us.* + a **fact** to support it (bones, plants).","**Other side (counterclaim):** *Some people say the night is cool and quiet. However, …* – the writer answers it.","**O – Opinion again (closing):** *For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!* – the opinion in new words.","**Opinion words:** *I believe, I think, in my opinion.* **Reason words:** *My first reason is that…, My second reason is that…*"]}],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"What is Omar's opinion?","answer":"Day is better than night.","explanation":"First sentence.","explanation_ar":"النهار أفضل.","options":["Night is better than day.","Day is better than night.","Football is boring.","The Moon is beautiful."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"What does the *O* at the start of OREO stand for?","answer":"Opinion","explanation":"OREO = Opinion, Reason, Example, Opinion.","explanation_ar":"الرأي.","options":["Orbit","Order","Opinion","Ocean"],"dok":1,"skill":"OREO","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which sentence is Omar's FIRST reason?","answer":"My first reason is that the day is full of action.","explanation":"Reason starter.","explanation_ar":"السبب الأول.","options":["My first reason is that the day is full of action.","For example, I can play football.","For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!","I believe day is better than night."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which sentence is an EXAMPLE?","answer":"For example, I can play football with my team in the park.","explanation":"For example.","explanation_ar":"مثال.","options":["I believe day is better.","For example, I can play football with my team in the park.","My second reason is that sunshine is good for us.","Some people say the night is cool."],"dok":1,"skill":"examples","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"A cool place out of the sun is ___.","answer":"shade","explanation":"Shade.","explanation_ar":"ظل.","options":["shade","sunlight","action","a reason"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which sentence is Omar's CLOSING?","answer":"For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!","explanation":"Opinion again.","explanation_ar":"الخاتمة.","options":["I read Layla's opinion.","My second reason is that sunshine is good for us.","However, I can sit in the shade.","For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!"],"dok":1,"skill":"closing","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS4-A2","type":"sequence","stage":"guided","instructions":"Put in order: Build an OREO paragraph.","instructions_ar":"ابنِ فقرة OREO.","items":[{"q":"Order the desert-trip paragraph.","answer":"I think the desert is the best place for a family trip. → My first reason is that the night sky is full of stars. → For example, we can see the Milky Way far from city lights. → My second reason is that families can camp and cook together. → For these reasons, I would choose the desert every time.","explanation":"O → R → E → R → O.","explanation_ar":"رأي ← سبب ← مثال ← سبب ← رأي.","stage":"guided","parts":["For these reasons, I would choose the desert every time.","My first reason is that the night sky is full of stars.","For example, we can see the Milky Way far from city lights.","My second reason is that families can camp and cook together.","I think the desert is the best place for a family trip."],"target":["I think the desert is the best place for a family trip.","My first reason is that the night sky is full of stars.","For example, we can see the Milky Way far from city lights.","My second reason is that families can camp and cook together.","For these reasons, I would choose the desert every time."]},{"q":"Build a reason sentence about reading.","answer":"My first reason → is that → reading makes → you smarter.","explanation":"Reason starter + that.","explanation_ar":"بداية السبب + that.","stage":"guided","parts":["you smarter.","is that","My first reason","reading makes"],"target":["My first reason","is that","reading makes","you smarter."]},{"q":"Build an opinion sentence about pets.","answer":"In my opinion, → cats make → better pets.","explanation":"Opinion starter + comma.","explanation_ar":"بداية الرأي + فاصلة.","stage":"guided","parts":["cats make","better pets.","In my opinion,"],"target":["In my opinion,","cats make","better pets."]},{"q":"Build an other-side sentence.","answer":"Some people say → night is → more peaceful.","explanation":"Other side.","explanation_ar":"الرأي الآخر.","stage":"guided","parts":["night is","more peaceful.","Some people say"],"target":["Some people say","night is","more peaceful."]},{"q":"Build an answer to the other side.","answer":"However, → the day → is full of → action.","explanation":"Answer with However.","explanation_ar":"الرد بـ However.","stage":"guided","parts":["the day","is full of","action.","However,"],"target":["However,","the day","is full of","action."]},{"q":"Build a closing about summer.","answer":"That is why → I love → the summer holiday.","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة.","stage":"guided","parts":["I love","the summer holiday.","That is why"],"target":["That is why","I love","the summer holiday."]}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS4-A3","type":"gap_fill","stage":"freer","instructions":"Freer practice: Use the word bank.","instructions_ar":"استخدم بنك الكلمات.","items":[{"q":"I ________ that every child should learn to swim.","answer":"believe","explanation":"Think it is right.","explanation_ar":"أعتقد.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"________, homework helps us practice.","answer":"In my opinion","explanation":"Opinion starter.","explanation_ar":"في رأيي.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"My first ________ is that swimming keeps you safe.","answer":"reason","explanation":"Why you think something.","explanation_ar":"سبب.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Plan your paragraph with ________: Opinion, Reason, Example, Opinion.","answer":"OREO","explanation":"The opinion plan.","explanation_ar":"خطة OREO.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"A football match is full of ________.","answer":"action","explanation":"Being busy and active.","explanation_ar":"حركة.","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Plants need ________ to grow.","answer":"sunlight","explanation":"Light from the Sun.","explanation_ar":"ضوء الشمس.","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS4-A4","type":"open","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write parts of an opinion paragraph.","instructions_ar":"اكتب أجزاء فقرة رأي.","items":[{"q":"Write your opinion: Is morning or evening better?","answer":"I think the morning is better than the evening.","explanation":"Opinion sentence.","explanation_ar":"جملة رأي.","dok":1,"skill":"opinion","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write two reasons with *My first reason is that… / My second reason is that…*","answer":"My first reason is that the air is fresh and cool. My second reason is that I have a lot of energy in the morning.","explanation":"Two reasons.","explanation_ar":"سببان.","dok":2,"skill":"reasons","stage":"production"},{"q":"Add an example or a fact to one reason.","answer":"For example, I can walk to the mosque for Fajr and see the sunrise.","explanation":"Support.","explanation_ar":"دعم.","dok":2,"skill":"support","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write a closing that says your opinion again in new words.","answer":"For these reasons, the morning is the best part of my day.","explanation":"Closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة.","dok":3,"skill":"closing","stage":"production"}]}],"game":{"name":"Build the OREO","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Cookie stacker: sentence cookies fall; the child stacks them in OREO order. Wrong order makes the cookie crumble; a perfect stack earns a 'Debate Star'.","Teams get mixed cookie cards for three topics.","They build three OREO stacks (one opinion, two reasons with examples, opinion again).","Each team reads one stack aloud with opinion and reason starters.","Other teams check the order and that reasons match the opinion.","Each correct stack = 3 points."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"An opinion paragraph tells ___.","answer":"what you think and why","explanation":"Opinion + reasons.","explanation_ar":"ما تعتقده ولماذا.","options":["what you think and why","only facts","a story with a problem","the steps to make something"],"dok":1,"skill":"genre"},{"q":"What does the *R* in OREO stand for?","answer":"Reason","explanation":"OREO.","explanation_ar":"السبب.","options":["Rocket","Read","Rest","Reason"],"dok":1,"skill":"OREO"},{"q":"Which of these sentence beginnings is an opinion starter?","answer":"I believe…","explanation":"Opinion words.","explanation_ar":"I believe.","options":["First, put…","I believe…","Long ago…","Dear Hamza,"],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion words"},{"q":"*Sit in the shade on hot days.* *Shade* is ___.","answer":"a cool place out of the sun","explanation":"Shade.","explanation_ar":"ظل.","options":["a bright light","a kind of hat","a cool place out of the sun","a reason"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence uses *In my opinion* correctly?","answer":"In my opinion, night is more peaceful.","explanation":"Comma after In my opinion.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["In my opinion night, is more peaceful.","In, my opinion night is peaceful.","In my opinion night is, peaceful.","In my opinion, night is more peaceful."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which reason supports *Every school should have a garden*?","answer":"Students can learn how plants grow.","explanation":"It explains why.","explanation_ar":"يدعم الرأي.","options":["Gardens are green.","Students can learn how plants grow.","I have a pencil.","The Moon has phases."],"dok":2,"skill":"reasons"},{"q":"Which sentence answers the other side correctly?","answer":"Some people say gardens are hard work. However, students enjoy working together.","explanation":"Other side + However.","explanation_ar":"يرد على الرأي الآخر.","options":["Gardens are hard work.","However gardens.","Some people say gardens are hard work. However, students enjoy working together.","Some people say gardens. The end."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterclaim"},{"q":"Why should every reason have an example or a fact?","answer":"to make the reason stronger and more believable","explanation":"Support persuades.","explanation_ar":"لتقوية السبب.","options":["to make the reason stronger and more believable","to make the paragraph shorter","to change the opinion","to add a heading"],"dok":3,"skill":"purpose"},{"q":"Which closing is BEST for *Cats make better pets*?","answer":"For these reasons, a cat is the perfect pet for a busy family.","explanation":"Restates the opinion.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة مناسبة.","options":["Dogs are nice too.","My first reason is that cats are quiet.","Cats.","For these reasons, a cat is the perfect pet for a busy family."],"dok":2,"skill":"closing"},{"q":"A partner's paragraph gives an opinion and two reasons but no examples. What should they add?","answer":"an example or a fact for each reason","explanation":"Support each reason.","explanation_ar":"مثال أو حقيقة لكل سبب.","options":["a second opinion that disagrees","a list of new words","an example or a fact for each reason","a story about a dragon"],"dok":3,"skill":"revising"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'believe': a child with a thumbs-up and a thought bubble"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'in my opinion': a speech bubble with 'In my opinion…'"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'reason': a child counting on fingers"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'action': children running and playing"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'sunlight': sunbeams on a playground"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'shade': a child under a tree out of the sun"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'OREO': a cookie-shaped organizer with four layers"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-01","prompt":"Omar plays football with his team on a sunny afternoon."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-02","prompt":"A cookie-shaped OREO organizer."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS4-03","prompt":"Students show agree or disagree cards."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V01","script":"believe. I believe day is better."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V02","script":"in my opinion. In my opinion, night is more peaceful."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V03","script":"reason. My first reason is that the day is full of action."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V04","script":"action. The day is full of action."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V05","script":"sunlight. Our bodies need sunlight."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V06","script":"shade. Sit in the shade on hot days."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-V07","script":"OREO. Use OREO to plan your paragraph."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-T1","script":"I read Layla's opinion, but I believe day is better than night. My first reason is that the day is full of action. For example, I can play football with my team in the park after school. My second reason is that sunshine is good for us. Our bodies need sunlight to make strong bones, and plants need it to grow food. Some people say the night is cool and quiet. However, I can sit in the shade and still enjoy the bright, busy day. For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!"},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Omar read Layla's opinion – and he does NOT agree! He writes his own. I read Layla's opinion, but I believe day is better than night. My first reason is that… OREO: Opinion, Reason, Example, Opinion again! Answer the other side: Some people say the night is cool. However, I can sit in the shade! End strong: For these reasons, the day will always be my favorite time!"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5","title":"Writing Workshop: Would I Like to Travel to Space?","lesson_type":"writing_workshop","objectives":["plan an opinion paragraph with the OREO / Argument Planner: opinion, reasons, evidence, the other side and the opinion restated","write 6–8 sentences answering 'Would I like to travel to space?' with two reasons, examples or facts, and a closing","revise for strong reasons, edit punctuation and publish the paragraph for a class 'Space Debate' wall"],"objectives_ar":["التخطيط لفقرة رأي بمخطط OREO/الحجة: الرأي والأسباب والأدلة والرأي الآخر وإعادة الرأي.","كتابة 6–8 جمل تجيب عن «هل أحب السفر إلى الفضاء؟» بسببين وأمثلة أو حقائق وخاتمة.","التحسين لتقوية الأسباب، وتدقيق الترقيم، والنشر على جدار «مناظرة الفضاء»."],"success_criteria":["I can state a clear opinion (yes or no).","I can give two reasons with an example or a fact for each.","I can answer the other side and restate my opinion."],"success_criteria_ar":["أستطيع ذكر رأي واضح (نعم أو لا).","أستطيع ذكر سببين مع مثال أو حقيقة لكل منهما.","أستطيع الرد على الرأي الآخر وإعادة رأيي."],"map_area":"Language Usage: Write, Revise Texts for Purpose and Audience (cross-strand)","vocabulary":[{"word":"space station","pos":"noun","ipa":"/speɪs ˈsteɪʃən/","definition":"a big spacecraft where astronauts live and work while it orbits Earth","arabic":"محطة فضائية","example":"Astronauts live on the space station for months.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V01","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V01","tier":"core"},{"word":"float","pos":"verb","ipa":"/floʊt/","definition":"to move gently in the air or on water without falling or sinking","arabic":"يطفو","example":"In space, astronauts float.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V02","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V02","tier":"core"},{"word":"dangerous","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdeɪndʒərəs/","definition":"able to hurt you; not safe","arabic":"خطير","example":"Some people say space is dangerous.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V03","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V03","tier":"core"},{"word":"train","pos":"verb","ipa":"/treɪn/","definition":"to practice and learn skills for a job or sport","arabic":"يتدرّب","example":"Astronauts train for years.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V04","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V04","tier":"core"},{"word":"explore","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ɪkˈsplɔr/","definition":"to travel to a new place to learn about it","arabic":"يستكشف","example":"I want to explore space.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V05","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V05","tier":"core"},{"word":"view","pos":"noun","ipa":"/vju/","definition":"what you can see from a place","arabic":"منظر","example":"The view of Earth from space is beautiful.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V06","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V06","tier":"core"},{"word":"homesick","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈhoʊmsɪk/","definition":"sad because you are far from home and family","arabic":"مشتاق إلى البيت","example":"An astronaut may feel homesick.","image_id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V07","audio_id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V07","tier":"core"}],"explanation":{"text":"Answer the question **Yes** or **No** in your **opinion sentence**. There is no wrong opinion – but you must **support** it.\n\nPlan with the **OREO / Argument Planner**: **Opinion** → **Reason 1 + example/fact** → **Reason 2 + example/fact** → **the other side** (*Some people say… However, …*) → **Opinion restated**.\n\nUse **facts** from the unit (the Earth spins, the Moon orbits, astronauts float) and real examples (Saudi astronauts). Use opinion and reason starters, **For example,** and **However,** with commas.","examples":["Opinion (yes): **I would love to travel to space one day.**","Reason 1: **My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above.**","Fact/example: **Astronauts say the view of our blue planet is the most beautiful thing they have ever seen.**","Reason 2: **My second reason is that I want to make my country proud.**","Fact: **In 2023, two Saudi astronauts, Rayyanah Barnawi and Ali AlQarni, traveled to the International Space Station.**","Other side: **Some people say space is dangerous.**","Answer: **However, astronauts train for years and wear special suits to stay safe.**","Closing: **For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!**","Opinion (no) example: **I would not like to travel to space because I would feel homesick, and I love to walk on the ground with my family.**"],"common_errors":["✗ Writing both yes and no. → ✓ Choose **one** opinion and support it. (One clear opinion.)","✗ Reasons with no support. → ✓ My first reason is that… For example, … (Add an **example** or a **fact**.)","✗ Some people say space is dangerous. (and nothing after) → ✓ …However, astronauts train for years. (**Answer** the other side.)","✗ I would like travel to space. → ✓ I would like to travel to space. (would like **to** + verb.)","✗ For example astronauts float. → ✓ For example, astronauts float. (Comma after **For example**.)","✗ Astronauts trains for years. → ✓ Astronauts train for years. (Many astronauts → **train**.)"],"arabic":"أجب عن السؤال بنعم أو لا في جملة الرأي، فلا يوجد رأي خاطئ، لكن يجب أن تدعمه.\n\nخطّط بمخطط OREO/الحجة: الرأي ← السبب الأول + مثال/حقيقة ← السبب الثاني + مثال/حقيقة ← الرأي الآخر والرد عليه ← إعادة الرأي.\n\nاستخدم حقائق من الوحدة وأمثلة حقيقية، مثل رائدَي الفضاء السعوديين ريانة برناوي وعلي القرني عام 2023.\n\nانتبه: would like to + فعل، وفاصلة بعد For example وHowever."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Would YOU like to travel to space? Sami says YES! Let's see how he plans his opinion.","on_screen":"Would I Like to Travel to Space? 🚀","visual":"Sami in a cardboard space helmet in front of a starry poster."},{"time":"00:20–00:55","narration":"Plan with OREO: opinion, two reasons with facts or examples, the other side, opinion again!","on_screen":"1 Plan – OREO / Argument Planner","visual":"An OREO stack with an extra 'other side' layer."},{"time":"00:55–01:55","narration":"I would love to travel to space one day. My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above…","on_screen":"2 Draft – opinion + reasons + support","visual":"Images: Earth from space; two Saudi astronauts waving from the space station (illustrated)."},{"time":"01:55–02:20","narration":"Revise: answer the other side! Some people say space is dangerous. However…","on_screen":"3 Revise – answer the other side","visual":"A see-saw tips back to Sami's opinion."},{"time":"02:20–02:40","narration":"Edit: would like TO, commas after For example and However.","on_screen":"4 Edit – to , ,","visual":"Missing words and commas fly into place."},{"time":"02:40–03:00","narration":"Publish: the class Space Debate wall – YES on one side, NO on the other!","on_screen":"5 Publish 🗳️","visual":"A wall split into YES and NO with students' paragraphs."}],"captions_ar":["هل تحب السفر إلى الفضاء؟ سامي يقول نعم! لنرَ كيف يخطط لرأيه.","خطّط بـ OREO: الرأي، وسببان بحقائق أو أمثلة، والرأي الآخر، ثم الرأي مرة أخرى!","أحب أن أسافر إلى الفضاء يومًا ما. سببي الأول أنني أريد أن أرى الأرض من الأعلى…","التحسين: رُدّ على الرأي الآخر! يقول بعضهم إن الفضاء خطير، ومع ذلك…","التدقيق: would like to، والفواصل بعد For example وHowever.","النشر: جدار مناظرة الفضاء في الفصل: «نعم» في جهة و«لا» في الأخرى!"],"voice":"Narrator: American English, warm female teacher, speed 0.90. Sami (the Questioner) reads his opinion with excitement."},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-A1","type":"mcq","stage":"controlled","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the best answer.","instructions_ar":"اختر أفضل إجابة.","items":[{"q":"Which sentence clearly states an opinion about space travel?","answer":"I would love to travel to space one day.","explanation":"Opinion = what you think.","explanation_ar":"رأي واضح.","options":["Space is big.","I would love to travel to space one day.","Rockets are white.","The Moon has phases."],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Where do astronauts live and work while orbiting Earth?","answer":"on a space station","explanation":"Space station.","explanation_ar":"محطة فضائية.","options":["on the Moon only","in a rocket on the ground","on a space station","in a desert camp"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Inside the space station, astronauts ___ in the air instead of walking.","answer":"float","explanation":"Float.","explanation_ar":"يطفون.","options":["sink","float","swim","dig"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Feeling sad because you are far from home is feeling ___.","answer":"homesick","explanation":"Homesick.","explanation_ar":"الشوق إلى البيت.","options":["dangerous","peaceful","proud","homesick"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which sentence about Saudi astronauts is a FACT?","answer":"In 2023, two Saudi astronauts traveled to the International Space Station.","explanation":"Checkable fact.","explanation_ar":"حقيقة.","options":["In 2023, two Saudi astronauts traveled to the International Space Station.","Space is the coolest place ever.","I think astronauts are lucky.","Everyone should go to space."],"dok":2,"skill":"fact vs. opinion","stage":"controlled"},{"q":"Which sentence answers the other side?","answer":"However, astronauts train for years and wear special suits.","explanation":"However + answer.","explanation_ar":"يرد على الرأي الآخر.","options":["Some people say space is dangerous.","I would love to travel to space.","My first reason is that I want to see Earth.","However, astronauts train for years and wear special suits."],"dok":2,"skill":"counterclaim","stage":"controlled"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-A2","type":"sequence","stage":"guided","instructions":"Put in order: Build the argument.","instructions_ar":"ابنِ الحجة.","items":[{"q":"Order Sami's argument.","answer":"I would love to travel to space one day. → My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above. → My second reason is that I want to make my country proud. → Some people say space is dangerous. → However, astronauts train for years. → For these reasons, I hope to explore space.","explanation":"Opinion → reasons → other side → answer → closing.","explanation_ar":"رأي ← أسباب ← رأي آخر ← رد ← خاتمة.","stage":"guided","parts":["I would love to travel to space one day.","My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above.","However, astronauts train for years.","Some people say space is dangerous.","For these reasons, I hope to explore space.","My second reason is that I want to make my country proud."],"target":["I would love to travel to space one day.","My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above.","My second reason is that I want to make my country proud.","Some people say space is dangerous.","However, astronauts train for years.","For these reasons, I hope to explore space."]},{"q":"Build a NO opinion sentence.","answer":"I would not → like to travel → to space.","explanation":"A NO opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي بالرفض.","stage":"guided","parts":["like to travel","I would not","to space."],"target":["I would not","like to travel","to space."]},{"q":"Build a NO reason.","answer":"My second reason → is that → I would feel → homesick.","explanation":"Reason starter.","explanation_ar":"بداية السبب.","stage":"guided","parts":["My second reason","homesick.","is that","I would feel"],"target":["My second reason","is that","I would feel","homesick."]},{"q":"Build an example for a NO reason.","answer":"For example, → astronauts cannot → eat with their families.","explanation":"Example + comma.","explanation_ar":"مثال + فاصلة.","stage":"guided","parts":["eat with their families.","astronauts cannot","For example,"],"target":["For example,","astronauts cannot","eat with their families."]},{"q":"Build an other-side sentence for a NO paragraph.","answer":"Some people say → space is → exciting.","explanation":"Other side (for a NO paragraph).","explanation_ar":"الرأي الآخر.","stage":"guided","parts":["exciting.","space is","Some people say"],"target":["Some people say","space is","exciting."]},{"q":"Build a NO closing.","answer":"For these reasons, → I will stay → on Earth!","explanation":"NO closing.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة الرفض.","stage":"guided","parts":["on Earth!","I will stay","For these reasons,"],"target":["For these reasons,","I will stay","on Earth!"]}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-A3","type":"organizer","stage":"freer","instructions":"Organizer: Plan your argument.","instructions_ar":"خطط لحجتك.","items":[{"q":"Opinion: YES or NO?","answer":"I would like to travel to space one day.","explanation":"Clear opinion.","explanation_ar":"رأي واضح.","dok":1,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Reason 1 + an example or a fact.","answer":"I want to float like an astronaut – astronauts float inside the space station and even sleep in bags on the wall.","explanation":"Reason + support.","explanation_ar":"سبب + دعم.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"Reason 2 + an example or a fact.","answer":"I want to see the Moon up close – it is a big ball of rock that reflects the Sun's light.","explanation":"Reason + support.","explanation_ar":"سبب + دعم.","dok":2,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"},{"q":"The other side + your answer, and your closing.","answer":"Some people say I would miss my family. However, I could call them every day. For these reasons…","explanation":"Other side + answer + closing.","explanation_ar":"رأي آخر + رد + خاتمة.","dok":3,"skill":"planning","stage":"freer"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-A4","type":"writing","stage":"production","instructions":"Writing: Write, revise, edit and publish your paragraph.","instructions_ar":"اكتب فقرتك وحسّنها ودققها وانشرها.","items":[{"q":"Write your opinion and your first reason with support.","answer":"I would love to travel to space one day. My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above. Astronauts say the view is the most beautiful thing they have ever seen.","explanation":"Opinion + reason 1 + support.","explanation_ar":"رأي + سبب أول + دعم.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write your second reason with support.","answer":"My second reason is that I want to make my country proud. For example, in 2023, two Saudi astronauts traveled to the space station.","explanation":"Reason 2 + support.","explanation_ar":"سبب ثانٍ + دعم.","dok":2,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Write the other side, your answer and your closing.","answer":"Some people say space is dangerous. However, astronauts train for years. For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!","explanation":"Other side + answer + closing.","explanation_ar":"رأي آخر + رد + خاتمة.","dok":3,"skill":"writing","stage":"production"},{"q":"Which reason did you make stronger after Pairs Check? How?","answer":"I added a fact about Saudi astronauts to my second reason.","explanation":"Revision note.","explanation_ar":"ملاحظة التحسين.","dok":3,"skill":"revising","stage":"production","_w":{"checklist":[],"min":null,"max":null}}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-ORG","type":"organizer","organizer":"OREO / Argument Planner","instructions":"Organizer: Write short notes for each part of your argument.","items":[{"q":"Opinion (yes or no)","answer":"I would love to travel to space one day."},{"q":"Reason 1 + example or fact","answer":"see the Earth from above – astronauts say the view is the most beautiful thing"},{"q":"Reason 2 + example or fact","answer":"make my country proud – in 2023, Saudi astronauts Rayyanah Barnawi and Ali AlQarni went to the space station"},{"q":"The other side: Some people say… However, …","answer":"space is dangerous – however, astronauts train for years and wear special suits"},{"q":"Opinion restated (closing)","answer":"For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!"}]},{"id":"RW-L03-U6-LS5-WR","type":"writing","instructions":"Writing: Write an opinion paragraph (6–8 sentences): \"Would I Like to Travel to Space?\" Give your opinion, two reasons with an example or a fact for each, answer the other side and restate your opinion. Write an opinion paragraph (6–8 sentences): \"Would I Like to Travel to Space?\" Give your opinion, two reasons with an example or a fact for each, answer the other side and restate your opinion.","instructions_ar":"اكتب فقرة رأي (6–8 جمل) بعنوان «هل أحب السفر إلى الفضاء؟»: اذكر رأيك وسببين مع مثال أو حقيقة لكل منهما، ورُدّ على الرأي الآخر، وأعد ذكر رأيك.","prompt":"Write an opinion paragraph (6–8 sentences): \"Would I Like to Travel to Space?\" Give your opinion, two reasons with an example or a fact for each, answer the other side and restate your opinion.","checklist":["My first sentence clearly says my opinion.","I gave two reasons with reason starters.","Each reason has an example or a fact.","I wrote the other side and answered it with However, …","My closing says my opinion again in new words.","I used commas after For example, However and In my opinion.","I used would like to + verb and at least three unit words."],"rubric_id":"RW-RUBRIC-5T","min_words":80,"max_words":160,"organizer":"OREO / Argument Planner (opinion → reasons → evidence → other side → opinion restated)","items":[{"q":"Write an opinion paragraph (6–8 sentences): \"Would I Like to Travel to Space?\" Give your opinion, two reasons with an example or a fact for each, answer the other side and restate your opinion.","answer":"I would love to travel to space one day. My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above. Astronauts say the view of our blue planet is the most beautiful thing they have ever seen. My second reason is that I want to make my country proud. For example, in 2023, two Saudi astronauts, Rayyanah Barnawi and Ali AlQarni, traveled to the International Space Station. Some people say space is dangerous. However, astronauts train for years and wear special suits to stay safe. For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!","_w":{"checklist":["My first sentence clearly says my opinion.","I gave two reasons with reason starters.","Each reason has an example or a fact.","I wrote the other side and answered it with However, …","My closing says my opinion again in new words.","I used commas after For example, However and In my opinion.","I used would like to + verb and at least three unit words."],"min":80,"max":160}}]}],"game":{"name":"Space Debate","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["On this screen: answer the lesson questions as fast as you can.","In class: Debate arena: the child chooses YES or NO, then picks the two strongest reasons and matching facts; the app plays the other side's point and the child chooses the best 'However' answer. Strong arguments launch a rocket or light up a house.","Split the class into YES and NO teams.","Each team chooses two reason cards and a matching fact or example for each.","Teams take turns reading one reason + support.","Each team must answer the other side with a 'However' card.","The teacher scores: clear reason (1), support (1), good 'However' answer (2)."],"data":[]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"What must an opinion paragraph have in the FIRST sentence?","answer":"a clear opinion","explanation":"Opinion first.","explanation_ar":"رأي واضح.","options":["a list of facts","a story beginning","a clear opinion","a date"],"dok":1,"skill":"structure"},{"q":"How many reasons should your paragraph give?","answer":"two","explanation":"Two reasons.","explanation_ar":"سببان.","options":["one","ten","two","none"],"dok":1,"skill":"structure"},{"q":"*Astronauts train for years.* *Train* here means ___.","answer":"practice and learn skills","explanation":"Train = practice.","explanation_ar":"يتدرّبون.","options":["practice and learn skills","ride a train","sleep","travel by bus"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary in context"},{"q":"*I want to explore space.* *Explore* means ___.","answer":"travel to a new place to learn about it","explanation":"Explore.","explanation_ar":"يستكشف.","options":["close a door","make a rocket","stay at home","travel to a new place to learn about it"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary"},{"q":"Which sentence about space travel is correct?","answer":"I would like to travel to space.","explanation":"would like to + verb.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["I would like travel to space.","I would like to traveling to space.","I would likes to travel to space.","I would like to travel to space."],"dok":2,"skill":"grammar"},{"q":"Which sentence about astronauts has the commas in the right places?","answer":"For example, astronauts float in the space station.","explanation":"Comma after For example.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["For example astronauts, float in the space station.","For example, astronauts float in the space station.","For, example astronauts float.","For example astronauts float, in space."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation"},{"q":"Which reason BEST supports *I would not like to travel to space*?","answer":"I would miss my family for many months.","explanation":"It explains the NO opinion.","explanation_ar":"يدعم الرفض.","options":["I would miss my family for many months.","Rockets are white.","The Moon has phases.","Stars are bright."],"dok":2,"skill":"reasons"},{"q":"Why should you answer the other side?","answer":"to show you thought about it and to make your argument stronger","explanation":"Counterclaim strengthens.","explanation_ar":"لتقوية حجتك.","options":["to change your opinion","to show you thought about it and to make your argument stronger","to make the paragraph confusing","to add a new topic"],"dok":3,"skill":"argument"},{"q":"Which closing is BEST for a YES paragraph?","answer":"For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!","explanation":"Restates the opinion.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة مناسبة.","options":["Some people say space is dangerous.","My first reason is that space is big.","For these reasons, I hope to explore space when I grow up!","Rockets are fast."],"dok":2,"skill":"closing"},{"q":"Which paragraph is the MOST convincing?","answer":"an opinion, two reasons with facts or examples, an answer to the other side and a closing","explanation":"Complete argument.","explanation_ar":"الأكثر إقناعًا.","options":["an opinion, two reasons with facts or examples, an answer to the other side and a closing","an opinion with no reasons","two opinions that disagree","a list of space words"],"dok":3,"skill":"evaluate"}],"images":[{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V01","prompt":"Picture for the word 'space station': the International Space Station above Earth"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V02","prompt":"Picture for the word 'float': an astronaut floating inside a spacecraft"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V03","prompt":"Picture for the word 'dangerous': a warning sign"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V04","prompt":"Picture for the word 'train': an astronaut training in a pool"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V05","prompt":"Picture for the word 'explore': a child with a map and a flashlight"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V06","prompt":"Picture for the word 'view': Earth seen from a spacecraft window"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V07","prompt":"Picture for the word 'homesick': a child looking at a family photo"},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-01","prompt":"Sami stands by a class debate wall about travelling to space."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-02","prompt":"An argument planner with five sections."},{"id":"IMG-RW-L03-U6-LS5-03","prompt":"Two illustrated astronauts float inside a space station."}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V01","script":"space station. Astronauts live on the space station for months."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V02","script":"float. In space, astronauts float."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V03","script":"dangerous. Some people say space is dangerous."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V04","script":"train. Astronauts train for years."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V05","script":"explore. I want to explore space."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V06","script":"view. The view of Earth from space is beautiful."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-V07","script":"homesick. An astronaut may feel homesick."},{"id":"AUD-RW-L03-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Would YOU like to travel to space? Sami says YES! Let's see how he plans his opinion. Plan with OREO: opinion, two reasons with facts or examples, the other side, opinion again! I would love to travel to space one day. My first reason is that I want to see the Earth from above… Revise: answer the other side! Some people say space is dangerous. However… Edit: would like TO, commas after For example and However. Publish: the class Space Debate wall – YES on one side, NO on the other!"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"Mars and Jupiter are ___.","answer":"planets","explanation":"They are planets.","explanation_ar":"كواكب.","options":["moons","planets","rockets","shadows"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"The Earth goes around the Sun. It ___ the Sun.","answer":"orbits","explanation":"Orbit = go around.","explanation_ar":"يدور حول.","options":["spins","orbits","reflects","floats"],"dok":1,"skill":"science words","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"A thin, curved moon is a ___.","answer":"crescent","explanation":"Crescent.","explanation_ar":"هلال.","options":["full moon","planet","phase only","crescent"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"When something blocks the light, it makes a ___.","answer":"shadow","explanation":"Shadow.","explanation_ar":"ظلًا.","options":["shadow","star","rocket","orbit"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"In a glossary of sky words, which word comes FIRST?","answer":"comet","explanation":"c comes first.","explanation_ar":"comet.","options":["planet","star","comet","orbit"],"dok":1,"skill":"ABC order","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which comes first in ABC order: *moon* or *month*?","answer":"month","explanation":"Third letter: n before o.","explanation_ar":"month.","options":["moon","They are the same.","month","Neither"],"dok":2,"skill":"ABC order","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*A **telescope** is a tool that makes faraway things look bigger.* What is a telescope?","answer":"a tool that makes faraway things look bigger","explanation":"Definition in the sentence.","explanation_ar":"تلسكوب.","options":["a tool that makes faraway things look bigger","a kind of planet","a shadow","a rocket"],"dok":1,"skill":"definition clues","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"*Observe the stars carefully.* *Observe* means ___.","answer":"watch carefully","explanation":"Observe = watch carefully.","explanation_ar":"ارصد.","options":["draw quickly","ignore","throw","watch carefully"],"dok":1,"skill":"vocabulary","_part":"Part A – Vocabulary"},{"q":"Which phrase starts an opinion sentence?","answer":"In my opinion,","explanation":"Opinion words.","explanation_ar":"In my opinion.","options":["Long ago,","In my opinion,","First, put","Dear Grandpa,"],"dok":1,"skill":"opinion words","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"},{"q":"Which reason sentence uses a reason starter correctly?","answer":"My first reason is that the stars are beautiful.","explanation":"is that + idea.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["My first reason the stars beautiful.","My first reason is that the stars are beautiful.","My first reason is the stars is beautiful.","First reason that beautiful stars."],"dok":1,"skill":"reasons","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence about day and night uses *However* correctly?","answer":"However, the night is cooler than the day.","explanation":"Comma after However.","explanation_ar":"صحيحة.","options":["However the night, is cooler.","The night however, is cooler however.","However; the night is cool.","However, the night is cooler than the day."],"dok":2,"skill":"punctuation","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"},{"q":"Which detail would BEST support *Every child should visit a planetarium*?","answer":"You can see the whole night sky on a big dome.","explanation":"Supports the opinion.","explanation_ar":"يدعم الرأي.","options":["You can see the whole night sky on a big dome.","Planetariums are buildings.","I like pizza.","The bus is yellow."],"dok":2,"skill":"support","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"},{"q":"Which sentence about Earth and sky is a FACT?","answer":"The Earth spins once every 24 hours.","explanation":"Checkable.","explanation_ar":"حقيقة.","options":["The night sky is the most beautiful thing.","Telescopes are the best gift.","The Earth spins once every 24 hours.","Space is boring."],"dok":1,"skill":"fact vs. opinion","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"},{"q":"Which closing is best for an opinion paragraph about telescopes?","answer":"For these reasons, every school should have a telescope.","explanation":"Restates the opinion.","explanation_ar":"خاتمة مناسبة.","options":["For these reasons, every school should have a telescope.","Some people say telescopes cost money.","My first reason is that telescopes are fun.","What is a telescope?"],"dok":2,"skill":"closing","_part":"Part D – Opinion writing skills"}],"unit_writing":{"task":"Which do you like more: the Sun or the Moon? Write an opinion paragraph with your opinion, two reasons with an example or a fact for each, the other side answered with However, and a closing.","model":"In my opinion, the Moon is more amazing than the Sun. My first reason is that the Moon changes its shape every night. For example, we can watch it grow from a thin crescent to a full moon in about two weeks. My second reason is that the crescent moon tells us when a new Islamic month begins, like Ramadan. Some people say the Sun is more important because it gives us light and heat. However, the Moon makes the night sky beautiful and helps us count our months. For these reasons, the Moon will always be my favorite!","marks":20}});
